    "d::core`\n\n    Whether `r` is `Err`, without consuming it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::core\u{1f}swap\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn swap<T>(ref<"
    "T, exclusive> a, ref<T, exclusive> b)\u{1f}Exchanges the values behind `a` and `b`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn swap<T>(re"
    "f<T, exclusive> a, ref<T, exclusive> b)\n    in `std::core`\n\n    Exchanges the values behind `a` and "
    "`b`.\n\n    A program cannot move a value out of a place it reaches through a reference, so it cannot "
    "exchange two\n    fields of a borrowed struct itself; this does. Nothing is copied or destroyed: a re"
    "source is now owned by\n    the place it is in. Each place is written as `*a = v` would write it: a l"
