    "t.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}Vec::from_raw\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Vec::from_raw<T: plain>(rawptr<T> p, usize n) : Vec"
    "<T>\u{1f}`n` elements of plain data copied from C memory into a `Vec`: a buffer a C caller owns, taken as"
    " a value the checks then cover (D-0257).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Vec::from_raw<T: plain>(rawptr<T> p, usize n) : "
    "Vec<T>\n    in `std::collections`\n    requires\n        n == 0 || p != null_rawptr<T>(), null_pointer,"
    " \"`Vec::from_raw`: `p` is C's `NULL`, where %v elements were to be copied from\", n\n\n    `n` elements"
    " of plain data copied from C memory into a `Vec`: a buffer a\n    C caller owns, taken as a value the"
    " checks then cover (D-0257). Called\n    inside `unsafe { }` (`[Trusted-Call]`): the caller vouches t"
    "hat the `n`\n    elements at `p` are readable and stay put for the call.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}Vec::from"
    "_c_bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Vec::from_c_bytes(rawptr<u8> p) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}A copy of the bytes C's text at `p` "
    "holds, up to and without its NUL.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Vec::from_c_bytes(rawptr<u8> p) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::"
    "collections`\n    requires\n        p != null_rawptr<u8>(), null_pointer, \"`p` is C's `NULL`, where te"
    "xt was expected (`String::from_c`, `Vec::from_c_bytes`)\"\n\n    A copy of the bytes C's text at `p` ho"
    "lds, up to and without its NUL.\n\n    Called only inside `unsafe`: `p` must point at readable bytes e"
    "nding in a NUL, as a C function's `char *`\n    result does. A null `p` faults (`null_pointer`); test"
    " with `is_null` first when C may return `NULL`.\n    `String::from_c` also checks that the bytes are "
    "UTF-8.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}Vec::from_fn\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Vec::from_fn<T>(usize n, fn(usize) : T f) : Vec<"
    "T>\u{1f}A new `Vec` of `f(0), f(1), …, f(n - 1)`, called in that order.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Vec::from_fn<T>(usiz"
    "e n, fn(usize) : T f) : Vec<T>\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    A new `Vec` of `f(0), f(1), …, f(n -"
    " 1)`, called in that order.\n\n    Works for any `T`, including resources.\n\n    Example, \"Vec::from_fn"
    ": with retain\":\n        Vec<i32> v = Vec::from_fn(6, [](usize i) : i32 { narrow<i32>(i) });\n        "
    "Vec::retain(&mut v, [](ref<i32, shared> x) : bool { *x % 2 == 0 });\n        assert(Vec::len(&v) == 3"
    ");\n        assert(v[0] == 0 && v[1] == 2 && v[2] == 4);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}Vec::append\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn "
