    "ool { *x > 5 }));\n        assert(Vec::all(&none, [](ref<i32, shared> x) : bool { *x > 5 }));\n       "
    " assert(Vec::count(&none, [](ref<i32, shared> x) : bool { *x > 5 }) == 0);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}slice_"
    "eq\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn slice_eq<T: eq>(slice<T, shared> a, slice<T, shared> b) : bool\u{1f}Whether `a` and `b` h"
    "ave the same length and equal elements in the same order.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn slice_eq<T: eq>(slice<T, shared"
    "> a, slice<T, shared> b) : bool\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    Whether `a` and `b` have the same len"
    "gth and equal elements in the same order.\n\n    Elements are compared with `==` in index order, stopp"
    "ing at the first difference. Slices have no `==`\n    of their own; a `Vec` is passed as `&v[0..$]`, "
    "an array as `&a[0..$]`.\n\n    Example, \"slice_eq: Vec and array\":\n        Vec<u8> v = Vec::new();\n   "
    "     Vec::push(&mut v, 1);\n        Vec::push(&mut v, 2);\n        array<u8, 2> a = [1, 2];\n        as"
