    "\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    A priority queue: it gives its elements back least first, in an orde"
    "r fixed when it is made.\n\n    `PriorityQueue::new` uses the key types' own order, `PriorityQueue::ne"
    "w_by` the caller's `less`.\n    Elements the order calls equal come out first in, first out. A binary"
    " heap: `push` and `pop` take time\n    in proportion to the logarithm of the length. The queue owns i"
    "ts elements. There is no `peek_mut`\n    (`pop`, change and `push` instead), no `foreach`, no `clone`"
    " and no `reserve`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}PriorityQueue::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::new<T>() : Prio"
    "rityQueue<T>\u{1f}A new, empty priority queue in the key types' own order, smallest first (as `Vec::sort`"
    " orders).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::new<T>() : PriorityQueue<T>\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    A new"
    ", empty priority queue in the key types' own order, smallest first (as `Vec::sort` orders).\n\n    `T`"
    " must be a key type or a float (in `Vec::sort`'s order, a NaN last); for any other `T` use\n    `Prio"
    "rityQueue::new_by`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}PriorityQueue::new_by\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::new_by<T>(f"
    "n(ref<T, shared>, ref<T, shared>) : bool less) : PriorityQueue<T>\u{1f}A new, empty priority queue in the"
    " order `less` gives: the element no other goes before comes out first.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::new"
    "_by<T>(fn(ref<T, shared>, ref<T, shared>) : bool less) : PriorityQueue<T>\n    in `std::collections`\n"
    "\n    A new, empty priority queue in the order `less` gives: the element no other goes before comes o"
    "ut\n    first.\n\n    `less` is true when its first argument goes before its second and must be a stric"
    "t weak order, as for\n    `Vec::sort_by`. A largest-first queue passes a `less` that answers \"greater"
    "\".\n\n    Example, \"PriorityQueue::new_by: first in, first out among equals\":\n        auto larger_tens"
    " = [](ref<i32, shared> a, ref<i32, shared> b) : bool { *a / 10 > *b / 10 };\n        PriorityQueue<i3"
    "2> q = PriorityQueue::new_by(larger_tens);\n        PriorityQueue::push(&mut q, 15);\n        Priority"
    "Queue::push(&mut q, 31);\n        PriorityQueue::push(&mut q, 12);\n        PriorityQueue::push(&mut q"
    ", 38);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)) == 31);\n        assert(Option::unwr"
    "ap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)) == 38);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)) == "
    "15);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)) == 12);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}PriorityQu"
    "eue::len\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::len<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, shared> q) : usize\u{1f}The number of e"
    "lements in `q`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::len<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, shared> q) : usize\n    in `st"
