    "collections`\n\n    Adds `x` to `q`; logarithmic in the length.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}PriorityQueue::pop\u{1f}"
    "fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::pop<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, exclusive> q) : Option<T>\u{1f}Removes the eleme"
    "nt that comes out first and returns it; `None` when `q` is empty.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::pop<T>(r"
    "ef<PriorityQueue<T>, exclusive> q) : Option<T>\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    Removes the element th"
    "at comes out first and returns it; `None` when `q` is empty.\n\n    Among elements the order calls equ"
    "al, the one pushed first comes out first. Logarithmic in the length.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}PriorityQueu"
    "e::peek\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::peek<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, shared> q) : Option<ref<T, shared>"
    ">\u{1f}The element `pop` would return next, as a shared reference; `None` when `q` is empty.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn P"
    "riorityQueue::peek<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, shared> q) : Option<ref<T, shared>>\n    in `std::collect"
    "ions`\n\n    The element `pop` would return next, as a shared reference; `None` when `q` is empty.\n\n  "
    "  The reference borrows the queue.\n\n    Example, \"PriorityQueue: smallest first\":\n        PriorityQu"
    "eue<i32> q = PriorityQueue::new();\n        PriorityQueue::push(&mut q, 5);\n        PriorityQueue::pu"
    "sh(&mut q, 1);\n        PriorityQueue::push(&mut q, 3);\n        assert(*Option::unwrap(PriorityQueue:"
    ":peek(&q)) == 1);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)) == 1);\n        assert(Op"
    "tion::unwrap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)) == 3);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PriorityQueue::pop(&mu"
    "t q)) == 5);\n        assert(Option::is_none(&PriorityQueue::pop(&mut q)));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}Priori"
    "tyQueue::clear\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PriorityQueue::clear<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, exclusive> q)\u{1f}Removes ever"
    "y element of `q`, destroying them in the order the heap holds them (not priority order).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn "
    "PriorityQueue::clear<T>(ref<PriorityQueue<T>, exclusive> q)\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    Removes e"
    "very element of `q`, destroying them in the order the heap holds them (not priority order).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::c"
    "ollections\u{1f}Vec::push_le\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Vec::push_le<T: integer>(ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> out, T x)\u{1f}Appe"
    "nds the `sizeof<T>()` bytes of `x` to `out`, least significant byte first (little-endian).\u{1f}\u{1f}export f"
    "n Vec::push_le<T: integer>(ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> out, T x)\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    Appends "
    "the `sizeof<T>()` bytes of `x` to `out`, least significant byte first (little-endian).\n\n    A signed"
    " `x` is written as its two's-complement image. `read_le` reads it back.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}Vec::push"
    "_be\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Vec::push_be<T: integer>(ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> out, T x)\u{1f}Appends the `sizeof<T>()"
