    "of<T>()` bytes of `x` to `out`, most significant byte first (big-endian, network order).\n\n    A sign"
    "ed `x` is written as its two's-complement image. `read_be` reads it back.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}read_le"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn read_le<T: integer>(slice<u8, shared> s, usize at) : T\u{1f}The `T` whose `sizeof<T>()` byt"
    "es start at `s[at]`, least significant byte first (little-endian).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn read_le<T: integer>(sl"
    "ice<u8, shared> s, usize at) : T\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    The `T` whose `sizeof<T>()` bytes st"
    "art at `s[at]`, least significant byte first (little-endian).\n\n    The type is written at the call: "
    "`read_le<u32>(&buf[0..$], 4)`. A signed `T` is read as two's\n    complement. Faults (`index_out_of_b"
    "ounds`) when fewer than `sizeof<T>()` bytes remain from `at`.\n\n    Example, \"read_le: round trip\":\n "
    "       Vec<u8> out = Vec::new();\n        Vec::push_be(&mut out, 0x0102: u16);\n        Vec::push_le(&"
    "mut out, -2: i16);\n        assert(out[0] == 0x01 && out[1] == 0x02 && out[2] == 0xfe && out[3] == 0x"
    "ff);\n        assert(read_be<u16>(&out, 0) == 0x0102);\n        assert(read_le<i16>(&out, 2) == -2);\n\u{1f}"
    "\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}read_be\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn read_be<T: integer>(slice<u8, shared> s, usize at) : T\u{1f}The `T"
    "` whose `sizeof<T>()` bytes start at `s[at]`, most significant byte first (big-endian).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn r"
    "ead_be<T: integer>(slice<u8, shared> s, usize at) : T\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    The `T` whose `"
    "sizeof<T>()` bytes start at `s[at]`, most significant byte first (big-endian).\n\n    The type is writ"
    "ten at the call: `read_be<u16>(&buf[0..$], 0)`. A signed `T` is read as two's\n    complement. Faults"
    " (`index_out_of_bounds`) when fewer than `sizeof<T>()` bytes remain from `at`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}sl"
    "ice_parts\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn slice_parts<T>(slice<T, exclusive> s, usize parts) : Vec<slice<T, exclusive>>"
    "\u{1f}Splits `s` into `parts` disjoint exclusive slices of consecutive elements, in order, as nearly equa"
    "l in length as they can be.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn slice_parts<T>(slice<T, exclusive> s, usize parts) : Vec<slic"
    "e<T, exclusive>>\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    Splits `s` into `parts` disjoint exclusive slices of"
    " consecutive elements, in order, as nearly equal in\n    length as they can be.\n\n    With `n` element"
    "s, each part has `n / parts` elements and the first `n % parts` parts one more; some are\n    empty w"
    "hen `parts > n`. The result is empty when `parts` is 0. The parts are disjoint, so each can be\n    g"
    "iven to a thread of its own (`spawn(work, part)`) and written there without a lock; the borrow of `s"
    "`\n    ends when the last part ends.\n\n    Example, \"slice_parts: lengths\":\n        array<i32, 5> a = "
    "[1, 2, 3, 4, 5];\n        Vec<slice<i32, exclusive>> parts = slice_parts(&mut a, 2);\n        assert(V"
    "ec::len(&parts) == 2);\n        assert(slice_len(parts[0]) == 3 && slice_len(parts[1]) == 2);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "collections\u{1f}slice_swap\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn slice_swap<T>(slice<T, exclusive> s, usize i, usize j)\u{1f}Exchanges"
    " elements `i` and `j` of `s`; nothing happens when `i == j`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn slice_swap<T>(slice<T, exclu"
    "sive> s, usize i, usize j)\n    in `std::collections`\n    requires\n        i < slice_len(s) && j < sl"
