    "ample, \"StringView::find: positions and the empty text\":\n        assert(StringView::contains(\"abc\", "
    "\"\"));\n        assert(StringView::find(\"abcabc\", \"c\") == Some(2: usize));\n        assert(StringView::"
    "find(\"abc\", \"d\") == None);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::starts_with\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::starts_with("
    "StringView v, StringView t) : bool\u{1f}Whether `v` begins with `t`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::starts_with(S"
    "tringView v, StringView t) : bool\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Whether `v` begins with `t`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}S"
    "tringView::ends_with\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::ends_with(StringView v, StringView t) : bool\u{1f}Whether `"
    "v` ends with `t`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::ends_with(StringView v, StringView t) : bool\n    in `std::t"
    "ext`\n\n    Whether `v` ends with `t`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::contains\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::conta"
    "ins(StringView v, StringView t) : bool\u{1f}Whether `t` occurs in `v`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::contains(St"
    "ringView v, StringView t) : bool\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Whether `t` occurs in `v`.\n\n    The empty t"
    "ext is in every text.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::trim_start\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::trim_start(StringV"
    "iew v) : StringView\u{1f}The view `v` without the ASCII white space at its start.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::"
    "trim_start(StringView v) : StringView\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The view `v` without the ASCII white s"
    "pace at its start.\n\n    White space is what `ascii_is_space` accepts.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::trim_e"
    "nd\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::trim_end(StringView v) : StringView\u{1f}The view `v` without the ASCII white"
    " space at its end.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::trim_end(StringView v) : StringView\n    in `std::text`\n\n  "
    "  The view `v` without the ASCII white space at its end.\n\n    White space is what `ascii_is_space` a"
    "ccepts.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::trim\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::trim(StringView v) : StringView\u{1f}The vi"
    "ew `v` without the ASCII white space at either end.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::trim(StringView v) : Stri"
    "ngView\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The view `v` without the ASCII white space at either end.\n\n    White "
    "space is what `ascii_is_space` accepts; there is no Unicode white space.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::spl"
    "it\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::split(StringView v, StringView sep) : Vec<StringView> from v\u{1f}The parts o"
    "f `v` between occurrences of `sep`, in order, each a view of the same text.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::s"
    "plit(StringView v, StringView sep) : Vec<StringView> from v\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The parts of `v`"
    " between occurrences of `sep`, in order, each a view of the same text.\n\n    Empty parts are kept: `\""
    "a,,b\"` gives three parts, and empty text one empty part. An empty `sep` gives `v`\n    whole. The par"
    "ts are views of `v` alone (`from v`), so `sep` is any text. `StringView::split_whitespace`\n    gives"
    " words without empty parts.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::split: empty fields\":\n        StringView line"
    " = \"a,,b\";\n        Vec<StringView> parts = StringView::split(line, \",\");\n        assert(Vec::len(&pa"
    "rts) == 3);\n        assert(parts[1] == \"\");\n        assert(parts[2] == \"b\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView:"
    ":char_count\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::char_count(StringView v) : usize\u{1f}The number of characters (code"
    " points) in `v`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::char_count(StringView v) : usize\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The"
    " number of characters (code points) in `v`.\n\n    `StringView::len` counts bytes; a character is one "
    "to four bytes. A character is a Unicode scalar value,\n    so `\"e\\u{301}\"` is two. Nothing is allocat"
    "ed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::chars\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::chars(StringView v) : Vec<StringView>\u{1f}The"
    " characters of `v`, in order, each a view of that character's one to four bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringVi"
    "ew::chars(StringView v) : Vec<StringView>\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The characters of `v`, in order, e"
    "ach a view of that character's one to four bytes.\n\n    Empty text gives an empty `Vec`. The `Vec` is"
    " new (one allocation); the views borrow what `v` borrows.\n    `StringView::code_point` reads a chara"
    "cter's code point, and `StringView::char_count` counts without the\n    `Vec`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView"
    "::replace\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::replace(StringView v, StringView from, StringView to) : String\u{1f}A "
    "new `String` holding `v` with every occurrence of `from` replaced by `to`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::re"
    "place(StringView v, StringView from, StringView to) : String\n    in `std::text`\n\n    A new `String` "
    "holding `v` with every occurrence of `from` replaced by `to`.\n\n    Occurrences are found left to rig"
    "ht and do not overlap; an empty `from` occurs nowhere, so the result is\n    then a copy of `v`.\n\n   "
    " Example, \"StringView::replace: no overlaps\":\n        String r = StringView::replace(\"aaa\", \"aa\", \"b"
    "\");\n        assert(r == \"ba\");\n        String same = StringView::replace(\"abc\", \"\", \"x\");\n        as"
    "sert(same == \"abc\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::join\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::join(slice<StringView, sh"
    "ared> parts, StringView sep) : String\u{1f}The texts of `parts`, in order, with `sep` between each two, i"
    "n a new `String`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::join(slice<StringView, shared> parts, StringView sep) : Str"
    "ing\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The texts of `parts`, in order, with `sep` between each two, in a new `S"
    "tring`.\n\n    No parts give an empty `String`. `String::join` joins a slice of `String`s.\n\n    Exampl"
    "e, \"StringView::join: separators between\":\n        Vec<StringView> parts = Vec::new();\n        Vec::"
    "push(&mut parts, StringView::of(\"a\"));\n        Vec::push(&mut parts, StringView::of(\"b\"));\n        V"
    "ec::push(&mut parts, StringView::of(\"c\"));\n        String j = StringView::join(&parts, \", \");\n      "
    "  assert(j == \"a, b, c\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::join\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::join(slice<String, shared> p"
    "arts, StringView sep) : String\u{1f}The texts of the `String`s in `parts`, in order, with `sep` between e"
    "ach two, in a new `String`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn String::join(slice<String, shared> parts, StringView sep) : S"
    "tring\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The texts of the `String`s in `parts`, in order, with `sep` between ea"
    "ch two, in a new `String`.\n\n    No parts give an empty `String`. `StringView::join` joins a slice of"
    " views.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::copy\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::copy(StringView v) : String\u{1f}A new `String` hol"
    "ding a copy of the text of `v`: a view, a `str`, a literal, or `&s` of a `String`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn String"
    "::copy(StringView v) : String\n    in `std::text`\n\n    A new `String` holding a copy of the text of `"
    "v`: a view, a `str`, a literal, or `&s` of a `String`.\n\n    `String::clone(&s)` copies a whole `Stri"
    "ng` the same way.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::chars: bytes and characters\":\n        String s = \"h\\u{e"
    "9}!\";\n        assert(StringView::len(&s) == 4);\n        assert(StringView::char_count(&s) == 3);\n   "
    "     Vec<StringView> cs = StringView::chars(&s);\n        assert(StringView::len(cs[1]) == 2);\n      "
    "  assert(StringView::code_point(cs[1]) == Some(0xe9: u32));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::strip_prefix\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn StringView::strip_prefix(StringView v, StringView t) : Option<StringView> from v\u{1f}The rest "
    "of `v` after `t` when `v` begins with `t`, else `None`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::strip_prefix(StringVi"
    "ew v, StringView t) : Option<StringView> from v\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The rest of `v` after `t` wh"
    "en `v` begins with `t`, else `None`.\n\n    It reads an option's value: `StringView::strip_prefix(a, \""
    "--name=\")` gives the value, or `None` for\n    another argument.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::strip_pre"
    "fix: an option's value\":\n        StringView a = \"--name=value\";\n        assert(Option::unwrap(String"
    "View::strip_prefix(a, \"--name=\")) == \"value\");\n        assert(Option::is_none(&StringView::strip_pre"
    "fix(a, \"--other=\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::strip_suffix\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::strip_suffix(Str"
    "ingView v, StringView t) : Option<StringView> from v\u{1f}The part of `v` before `t` when `v` ends with `"
    "t`, else `None`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::strip_suffix(StringView v, StringView t) : Option<StringView"
    "> from v\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The part of `v` before `t` when `v` ends with `t`, else `None`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}s"
    "td::text\u{1f}StringView::lines\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::lines(StringView v) : Vec<StringView>\u{1f}The lines "
    "of `v`: the parts between `\\n` bytes, each without a `\\r` just before its `\\n`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringVie"
    "w::lines(StringView v) : Vec<StringView>\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The lines of `v`: the parts between"
    " `\\n` bytes, each without a `\\r` just before its `\\n`.\n\n    There is no empty line after a final `\\n"
    "`, so `\"a\\nb\\n\"` and `\"a\\nb\"` both give `a` and `b`; `\"\\n\\n\"`\n    gives two empty lines, and empty t"
    "ext none. A `\\r` not followed by `\\n` stays in its line.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::lines: line endi"
    "ngs\":\n        StringView text = \"one\\r\\ntwo\\n\\nthree\\n\";\n        Vec<StringView> ls = StringView::li"
    "nes(text);\n        assert(Vec::len(&ls) == 4);\n        assert(ls[0] == \"one\");\n        assert(ls[2] "
    "== \"\");\n        assert(ls[3] == \"three\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::split_whitespace\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Stri"
    "ngView::split_whitespace(StringView v) : Vec<StringView>\u{1f}The words of `v`: the runs of bytes that ar"
    "e not ASCII white space, in order.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::split_whitespace(StringView v) : Vec<Strin"
    "gView>\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The words of `v`: the runs of bytes that are not ASCII white space, i"
    "n order.\n\n    No word is empty, so leading, trailing and repeated white space make no difference. Wh"
    "ite space is what\n    `ascii_is_space` accepts.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::split_whitespace: runs of"
    " spaces\":\n        Vec<StringView> w = StringView::split_whitespace(\"  to  be\\tor \");\n        assert("
    "Vec::len(&w) == 3);\n        assert(w[0] == \"to\");\n        assert(w[2] == \"or\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringVi"
    "ew::code_point\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::code_point(StringView v) : Option<u32>\u{1f}The code point of the"
    " first character of `v`, or `None` when `v` is empty.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::code_point(StringView v"
    ") : Option<u32>\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The code point of the first character of `v`, or `None` when"
    " `v` is empty.\n\n    With `StringView::chars`, it reads every character of a text in turn.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tex"
    "t\u{1f}String::push_code_point\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::push_code_point(ref<String, exclusive> s, u32 cp)\u{1f}App"
    "ends the character with code point `cp` to `s`, as one to four UTF-8 bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn String::push_"
    "code_point(ref<String, exclusive> s, u32 cp)\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Appends the character with code"
    " point `cp` to `s`, as one to four UTF-8 bytes.\n\n    A value that is no character (a surrogate, `0xD"
    "800` to `0xDFFF`, or above `0x10FFFF`) appends U+FFFD, the\n    replacement character, so `s` stays U"
    "TF-8.\n\n    Example, \"String::push_code_point: a surrogate\":\n        String s = String::new();\n      "
    "  String::push_code_point(&mut s, 0x41);\n        String::push_code_point(&mut s, 0xD800);\n        as"
    "sert(s == \"A\\u{fffd}\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::parse<T>(StringView v"
    ") : Result<T, ParseError>\u{1f}The number the text of `v` holds, as a `T`: an integer type, `f32` or `f64"
    "`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::parse<T>(StringView v) : Result<T, ParseError>\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The"
    " number the text of `v` holds, as a `T`: an integer type, `f32` or `f64`.\n\n    Parsed in place, by t"
    "he rules and with the errors of `[Parse]` (spec/21 §2d): the whole text or nothing, so white\n    sp"
    "ace around the number must be trimmed first.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::parse_radix\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String"
    "View::parse_radix<T: integer>(StringView v, u32 radix) : Result<T, ParseError>\u{1f}The integer the text "
    "of `v` writes in base `radix` (2 to 36), as a `T`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::parse_radix<T: integer>(St"
    "ringView v, u32 radix) : Result<T, ParseError>\n    in `std::text`\n    requires\n        radix >= 2 &&"
    " radix <= 36, assert_failed, \"StringView::parse_radix: the radix is from 2 to 36, not %v\", radix\n\n  "
    "  The integer the text of `v` writes in base `radix` (2 to 36), as a `T`.\n\n    Digits are `0`-`9` th"
    "en `a`-`z` or `A`-`Z`, with no prefix such as `0x`; a leading `-` for a signed `T`.\n    The whole te"
    "xt or nothing, as `StringView::parse`: `Err(Empty)`, `Err(Invalid(position))` for a character\n    th"
    "at is no digit of the base, `Err(OutOfRange)` when the number does not fit. A radix outside 2 to 36 "
    "is\n    a fault.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::parse_radix: bases, signs and errors\":\n        assert(Str"
    "ingView::parse_radix<u8>(\"ff\", 16) == Ok(255));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u8>(\"FF\", 16)"
    " == Ok(255));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u8>(\"100\", 16) == Err(OutOfRange));\n        ass"
    "ert(StringView::parse_radix<i8>(\"-80\", 16) == Ok(-128));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<i8>("
    "\"80\", 16) == Err(OutOfRange));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u32>(\"777\", 8) == Ok(511));\n  "
    "      assert(StringView::parse_radix<u64>(\"1010\", 2) == Ok(10));\n        assert(StringView::parse_ra"
    "dix<u32>(\"zz\", 36) == Ok(1295));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u32>(\"12g\", 16) == Err(Inval"
    "id(2)));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u32>(\"-1\", 16) == Err(Invalid(0)));\n        assert(S"
    "tringView::parse_radix<i32>(\"-\", 10) == Err(Invalid(1)));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u32"
    ">(\"\", 10) == Err(Empty));\n\n    Example, \"StringView::parse: no white space\":\n        StringView v = "
    "\" 42 \";\n        assert(StringView::parse<u32>(v) == Err(Invalid(0)));\n        assert(StringView::par"
    "se<u32>(StringView::trim(v)) == Ok(42));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::append\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::append<T>(r"
    "ef<String, exclusive> s, T x)\u{1f}Appends `x` to `s` as text: the bytes `printf(\"%v\", x)` would write.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "export fn String::append<T>(ref<String, exclusive> s, T x)\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Appends `x` to `s"
    "` as text: the bytes `printf(\"%v\", x)` would write.\n\n    `x` is a `str`, a `StringView`, a `ref<Stri"
    "ng, shared>`, an integer, `f32`, `f64` or `bool`; another type\n    is rejected at the call. A float "
    "is written in the shortest digits that read back as the same value\n    (`1.0`, `0.1`). `String::appe"
    "ndf` appends formatted text.\n\n    Example, \"String::append: numbers as printf writes them\":\n        "
    "String s = \"x = \";\n        String::append(&mut s, 1.0);\n        String::append(&mut s, \", n = \");\n  "
    "      String::append(&mut s, 42: u8);\n        assert(s == \"x = 1.0, n = 42\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::fr"
    "om_view\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::from_view\u{1f}\u{1f}removed\u{1f}export fn String::from_view\n    in `std::text`\n    r"
    "emoved: write String::copy(…): a copy of a view's text (D-0312)\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::to_ascii_lower"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::to_ascii_lower\u{1f}\u{1f}removed\u{1f}export fn String::to_ascii_lower\n    in `std::text`\n  "
    "  removed: write StringView::to_ascii_lower(&s): it takes the text's view (D-0312)\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}Strin"
    "g::to_ascii_upper\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::to_ascii_upper\u{1f}\u{1f}removed\u{1f}export fn String::to_ascii_upper\n    "
