    "port unsafe extern fn arg_bytes(usize i, rawptr<u8> buf, usize len) : isize\n    in `std::env`\n\n    C"
    "opies at most `len` bytes of argument `i` to `buf` and returns the argument's whole length.\n\n    Ret"
    "urns -1, storing nothing, when there is no argument `i`; a call with `len` 0 only asks whether\n    a"
    "rgument `i` exists and how long it is. Called inside `unsafe`: `[buf, buf + len)` must be storage\n  "
    "  outside every live object. For an argument's bytes whatever they are; `arg` is the safe way to rea"
    "d one.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}arg_count\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn arg_count() : usize\u{1f}The number of the program's arguments, "
