    "r of the program's arguments, not counting the program's own name.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}arg\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn arg(u"
    "size i) : Result<String, Utf8Error>\u{1f}Argument `i` of the program, counted from 0 for the first after "
    "the program's own name.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn arg(usize i) : Result<String, Utf8Error>\n    in `std::env`\n\n    A"
    "rgument `i` of the program, counted from 0 for the first after the program's own name.\n\n    `Err(e)`"
    " when the argument is not UTF-8, `e.offset` being the bad byte's offset within it; use\n    `arg_byte"
    "s` for such an argument. Faults (`index_out_of_bounds`) when `i >= arg_count()`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}env_var\u{1f}"
