    "nt variable `name`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn env_var(StringView name) : Result<Option<String>, Utf8Error>\n    in `"
    "std::env`\n\n    The value of the environment variable `name`.\n\n    `Ok(None)` when it is not set; `Er"
    "r(e)` when its value is not UTF-8, `e` giving the offset of the first\n    byte that is not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::e"
    "nv\u{1f}current_dir\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn current_dir() : Result<String, FileError>\u{1f}The working directory, against"
    " which a relative path is resolved.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn current_dir() : Result<String, FileError>\n    in `std"
    "::env`\n\n    The working directory, against which a relative path is resolved.\n\n    `Err(Utf8(e))` wh"
    "en its name is not UTF-8.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}set_current_dir\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn set_current_dir(StringView path) :"
    " Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Makes `path` the working directory, against which relative paths are resolv"
    "ed from now on.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn set_current_dir(StringView path) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::e"
    "nv`\n\n    Makes `path` the working directory, against which relative paths are resolved from now on.\n"
    "\n    The change is seen by every thread of the program.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}temp_dir\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn temp_dir() "
