    "ec::len(&rest) == 1 && rest[0] == \"in.txt\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args::flag\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Args::flag(ref<Args,"
    " exclusive> a, str name, str short, str help) : bool\u{1f}Whether `--name` or `-short` is among the argum"
    "ents before `--`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::flag(ref<Args, exclusive> a, str name, str short, str help) : boo"
    "l\n    in `std::env`\n    requires\n        StringView::len(&Args::clash(a, name, short)) == 0, assert_"
    "failed, \"%s\", &Args::clash(a, name, short)\n\n    Whether `--name` or `-short` is among the arguments "
    "before `--`.\n\n    `short` is one letter, or `\"\"` for none; `help` is the option's line in `Args::hel"
    "p`. Every occurrence\n    is taken, so `Args::finish` does not see it. Faults (`assert_failed`) when "
    "an earlier declaration has the\n    same name or the same letter (the first would take every occurren"
    "ce).\n\n    Example, \"Args::flag: after --\":\n        Vec<String> items = Vec::new();\n        Vec::push"
    "(&mut items, \"--\");\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"-v\");\n        Args a = Args::from(items, \"prog [o"
    "ptions] FILE\");\n        assert(!Args::flag(&mut a, \"verbose\", \"v\", \"say more\"));\n        Vec<String>"
    " rest = Result::unwrap(Args::finish(&mut a));\n        assert(Vec::len(&rest) == 1 && rest[0] == \"-v\""
