    "== 0, assert_failed, \"%s\", &Args::clash(a, name, short)\n\n    Every value given for the option `--nam"
    "e` or `-short`, in order.\n\n    A value is given as `--name=value`, `--name value` or `-s value`; eac"
    "h is taken, the value with it.\n    `value_name` names the value in `Args::help` (`FILE`). A `--name`"
    " or `-s` that is the last argument,\n    just before `--`, or followed by an argument an earlier decl"
    "aration took (a flag's `-v`), has no value\n    and is left for `Args::finish` to refuse. Faults (`as"
    "sert_failed`) when an earlier declaration has the\n    same name or the same letter.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args:"
    ":command\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Args::command(ref<Args, exclusive> a, str value_options) : Vec<String>\u{1f}Takes t"
    "he command of a git-style program and the arguments after it: `tool -v commit -m hi` gives `commit -"
    "m hi`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::command(ref<Args, exclusive> a, str value_options) : Vec<String>\n    in `std"
    "::env`\n\n    Takes the command of a git-style program and the arguments after it: `tool -v commit -m "
    "hi` gives\n    `commit -m hi`.\n\n    Called before the program's own options are declared. The command"
    " is the first argument (before `--`, or\n    just after it) that does not start with `-` and is not t"
    "he value of one of `value_options`, the options\n    written there that take a value (`\"-C --config\"`"
    ", as they are written before the command; `\"\"` for none).\n    It and every argument after it are tak"
    "en, so the declarations that follow read only the arguments before\n    it and `Args::finish` gives n"
    "one of them; the command's own options are read with\n    `Args::from(cmd, \"tool commit [options]\")`,"
    " whose `finish` gives the command first. Empty when there is no\n    command.\n\n    Example, \"Args::co"
    "mmand: git-style\":\n        Vec<String> items = Vec::new();\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"-C\");\n    "
    "    Vec::push(&mut items, \"dir\");\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"-v\");\n        Vec::push(&mut items,"
    " \"commit\");\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"-v\");\n        Vec::push(&mut items, \"-m\");\n        Vec::p"
    "ush(&mut items, \"hello\");\n        Args a = Args::from(items, \"tool [-v] [-C DIR] COMMAND\");\n        "
    "Vec<String> cmd = Args::command(&mut a, \"-C --dir\");\n        bool verbose = Args::flag(&mut a, \"verb"
    "ose\", \"v\", \"say more\");\n        Option<String> dir = Args::option(&mut a, \"dir\", \"C\", \"DIR\", \"where "
    "to work\");\n        assert(verbose && Option::unwrap(dir) == \"dir\");\n        assert(Vec::len(&Result:"
    ":unwrap(Args::finish(&mut a))) == 0);\n        Args c = Args::from(cmd, \"tool commit [-v] -m MSG\");\n "
    "       bool cv = Args::flag(&mut c, \"verbose\", \"v\", \"show the diff\");\n        Option<String> msg = A"
    "rgs::option(&mut c, \"message\", \"m\", \"MSG\", \"the message\");\n        Vec<String> rest = Result::unwrap"
    "(Args::finish(&mut c));\n        assert(cv && Option::unwrap(msg) == \"hello\" && Vec::len(&rest) == 1 "
    "&& rest[0] == \"commit\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args::option\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Args::option(ref<Args, exclusive> a, s"
    "tr name, str short, str value_name, str help) : Option<String>\u{1f}The value of the option `--name` or `"
    "-short`, the last one when it is given more than once.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::option(ref<Args, exclusive> "
    "a, str name, str short, str value_name, str help) : Option<String>\n    in `std::env`\n\n    The value "
    "of the option `--name` or `-short`, the last one when it is given more than once.\n\n    `None` when i"
    "t is not given. Takes its arguments as `Args::options` does.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args::finish\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Ar"
    "gs::finish(ref<Args, exclusive> a) : Result<Vec<String>, String>\u{1f}The arguments no declaration took, "
    "in order, every argument after `--` among them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::finish(ref<Args, exclusive> a) : Re"
    "sult<Vec<String>, String>\n    in `std::env`\n\n    The arguments no declaration took, in order, every "
    "argument after `--` among them.\n\n    `Err(message)` for the first argument before `--` that starts w"
    "ith `-` and is not a lone `-`:\n    `unknown option --x`; `missing a value for --x` for a declared op"
    "tion given without its value; and for a\n    declared option written in a form that is not read, the "
    "form to write: `-I takes its value as a separate\n    argument: -I inc` for `-Iinc`, `short options a"
    "re written one at a time: -v -o` for `-vo`, `--verbose\n    takes no value` for `--verbose=yes`. The "
    "message is for the program to print, usually followed by\n    `Args::help`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::env\u{1f}Args::help\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn Args::help(ref<Args, shared> a) : String\u{1f}The usage line and one aligned line per option de"
    "clared so far, ready to print.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Args::help(ref<Args, shared> a) : String\n    in `std::env`"
    "\n\n    The usage line and one aligned line per option declared so far, ready to print.\n\n    Example, "
    "\"Args::help: the layout\":\n        Args a = Args::from(Vec::new(), \"prog FILE\");\n        bool verbose"
    " = Args::flag(&mut a, \"verbose\", \"v\", \"say more\");\n        Option<String> out = Args::option(&mut a,"
    " \"out\", \"\", \"FILE\", \"where to write\");\n        String h = Args::help(&a);\n        assert(h == \"Usage"
    ": prog FILE\\n\\nOptions:\\n\"\n                    \"  -v, --verbose   say more\\n\"\n                    \" "
    "     --out FILE  where to write\\n\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct Rc<T>\u{1f}A referenc"
    "e-counted handle to a value on the heap that several owners in one thread share.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource st"
    "ruct Rc<T>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A reference-counted handle to a value on the heap that several "
    "owners in one thread share.\n\n    Each `Rc` is one strong handle; the value is destroyed when the las"
    "t strong handle is, and the memory is\n    freed once no `Weak` handle remains either. The value is r"
    "eached only as a shared reference (`Rc::get`),\n    so changing it needs a `mutex` inside. A cycle of"
    " `Rc`s is never freed: a parent pointer, a cache or an\n    observer list holds a `Weak` instead. `Rc"
    "` is not thread-safe (the count is not synchronised), so `spawn`\n    refuses one, or a value holding"
    " or referring to one (`diag.not-thread-safe`), and an `Rc` or `Weak` used in\n    a thread other than"
    " the one that made it (carried there by a closure the compiler could not see through)\n    faults wit"
    "h the same diagnostic; share across threads with `Arc<T>` or `ref<mutex<T>, shared>`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}"
    "Rc::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rc::new<T>(T v) : Rc<T>\u{1f}A new `Rc` holding `v`, the only strong handle to it.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "export fn Rc::new<T>(T v) : Rc<T>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A new `Rc` holding `v`, the only strong "
    "handle to it.\n\n    Allocates; faults (`alloc_failure`) when memory cannot be had.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc::"
    "clone\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rc::clone<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r) : Rc<T>\u{1f}A second strong handle to the value `r"
    "` holds; nothing is copied.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rc::clone<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r) : Rc<T>\n    in `std::memor"
    "y`\n\n    A second strong handle to the value `r` holds; nothing is copied.\n\n    What `clone(&r)` call"
    "s for an `Rc`. A reference into the value from `Rc::get` may stay live across it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc::"
    "get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rc::get<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r) : ref<T, shared>\u{1f}The value `r` holds, as a shared "
    "reference.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rc::get<T>(ref<Rc<T>, shared> r) : ref<T, shared>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    Th"
    "e value `r` holds, as a shared reference.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc::drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rc::drop<T>(ref<Rc<T>,"
    " exclusive> self)\u{1f}Ends one strong handle; run when an `Rc` is destroyed, so programs write `drop(r)`"
    " or let it go.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rc::drop<T>(ref<Rc<T>, exclusive> self)\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    Ends one"
    " strong handle; run when an `Rc` is destroyed, so programs write `drop(r)` or let it go.\n\n    When t"
    "his was the last strong handle the value is destroyed now, and with no `Weak` handle left the\n    me"
    "mory is freed too.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Weak\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct Weak<T>\u{1f}A handle to an `Rc`'s va"
    "lue that does not keep the value alive.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct Weak<T>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A "
    "handle to an `Rc`'s value that does not keep the value alive.\n\n    It keeps only the memory: once th"
    "e last `Rc` ends, the value is gone and `Weak::upgrade` gives `None`.\n    Dropping the last handle o"
    "f either kind frees the memory.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memory\u{1f}Rc::downgrade\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rc::downgrade<T>(ref<Rc<T>,"
    " shared> r) : Weak<T>\u{1f}A `Weak` handle to the value `r` holds.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rc::downgrade<T>(ref<Rc<T>,"
    " shared> r) : Weak<T>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A `Weak` handle to the value `r` holds.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::memor"
    "y\u{1f}Weak::upgrade\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Weak::upgrade<T>(ref<Weak<T>, shared> w) : Option<Rc<T>>\u{1f}A new strong h"
    "andle to the value, or `None` when the value has ended.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Weak::upgrade<T>(ref<Weak<T>, sha"
    "red> w) : Option<Rc<T>>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A new strong handle to the value, or `None` when t"
    "he value has ended.\n\n    The value never comes back once ended: after the last `Rc` is destroyed eve"
    "ry upgrade gives `None`.\n\n    Example, \"Weak::upgrade: after the last Rc\":\n        Rc<String> a = Rc"
    "::new(\"shared\");\n        Rc<String> b = Rc::clone(&a);\n        assert(StringView::len(Rc::get(&b)) ="
    "= 6);\n        Weak<String> w = Rc::downgrade(&a);\n        drop(a);\n        assert(Option::is_some(&W"
    "eak::upgrade(&w)));\n        drop(b);\n        assert(Option::is_none(&Weak::upgrade(&w)));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::mem"
    "ory\u{1f}Weak::clone\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Weak::clone<T>(ref<Weak<T>, shared> w) : Weak<T>\u{1f}A second `Weak` handle"
    " to the same value; what `clone(&w)` calls for a `Weak`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Weak::clone<T>(ref<Weak<T>, shar"
    "ed> w) : Weak<T>\n    in `std::memory`\n\n    A second `Weak` handle to the same value; what `clone(&w)"
