    "ailure as a value instead of raising it again.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn try_join<R>(handle<R> h) : Result<R, Threa"
    "dFailure>\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Waits for the thread `h` and gives its result, or its failure as a"
    " value instead of raising it again.\n\n    `Ok` of the thread's result; `Err(ThreadFailure)` when the "
    "thread faulted or was cancelled, and the\n    failure is then taken, so nothing is raised. How a supe"
    "rvisor keeps going when a worker has a bug; `join`\n    raises the failure instead.\n\n    Example, \"tr"
    "y_join: a contained fault\":\n        Option<i32> none = None;\n        auto h = spawn(Option::unwrap<i"
    "32>, none);\n        match (try_join(h))\n        {\n            Ok(_)  : assert(false),\n            Er"
