    "very memory access before it, in this thread, is ordered before every one after it, as seen by any o"
    "ther thread or device.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn atomic_fence()\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A full memory fence: every "
    "memory access before it, in this thread, is ordered before every one after it,\n    as seen by any ot"
    "her thread or device.\n\n    CobaltC's own operations are already sequentially consistent, so a progra"
    "m that stays within them never\n    needs this. It is for raw and volatile accesses and C code, which"
    " are outside that guarantee: the\n    equivalent of C's `atomic_thread_fence(memory_order_seq_cst)`.\n"
    "\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}spin_hint\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn spin_hint()\u{1f}Tells the processor that this thread is spinning, wai"
    "ting for another thread to change something.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn spin_hint()\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Tells th"
    "e processor that this thread is spinning, waiting for another thread to change something.\n\n    The C"
    "PU's pause instruction: it saves power and lets the other hardware thread of the core run. Call it i"
    "n\n    the body of a loop that polls an atomic; `Atomic::wait` blocks instead, for waits that may be "
    "long.\n\n    Example, \"Atomic::fetch_max: extremes and updates\":\n        Atomic<i32> a = Atomic::new(1"
    "0: i32);\n        assert(Atomic::fetch_max(&a, 4) == 10);\n        assert(Atomic::fetch_max(&a, 25) =="
    " 10);\n        assert(Atomic::fetch_min(&a, 30) == 25);\n        assert(Atomic::fetch_min(&a, -3) == 2"
    "5);\n        assert(Atomic::load(&a) == -3);\n        assert(Result::unwrap(Atomic::fetch_update(&a, ["
    "](i32 x) : Option<i32> { Some(x * 2) })) == -3);\n        match (Atomic::fetch_update(&a, [](i32 x) :"
    " Option<i32> { None }))\n        {\n            Ok(_)  : assert(false),\n            Err(v) : assert(v "
    "== -6),\n        }\n\n    Example, \"Atomic::wait: woken by notify_all\":\n        AtomicBool done = Atomi"
    "cBool::new(false);\n        {\n            handle<void> h = spawn(move [](ref<AtomicBool, shared> d)\n "
    "           {\n                AtomicBool::store(d, true);\n                AtomicBool::notify_all(d);\n"
    "            }, &done);\n            AtomicBool::wait(&done, false);\n            join(h);\n        }\n  "
    "      assert(AtomicBool::load(&done));\n        assert(AtomicBool::swap(&done, false));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}B"
    "arrier\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Barrier\u{1f}A meeting point for a fixed number of threads.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Ba"
    "rrier\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A meeting point for a fixed number of threads.\n\n    Shared by referenc"
    "e, as a `mutex` is. `Barrier::wait` blocks until `parties` threads have called it, then\n    releases"
    " them all together and is ready for the next round: the phases of a parallel algorithm, where\n    ev"
    "ery thread must finish one before any starts the next.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Barrier::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Barrier"
    "::new(usize parties) : Barrier\u{1f}A barrier for `parties` threads.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Barrier::new(usize partie"
    "s) : Barrier\n    in `std::sync`\n    requires\n        parties != 0, barrier_zero_parties\n\n    A barri"
    "er for `parties` threads.\n\n    Faults (`barrier_zero_parties`) when `parties` is 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Barr"
    "ier::wait\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Barrier::wait(ref<Barrier, shared> b) : bool\u{1f}Waits until `parties` threads ha"
    "ve called it, then lets them all go on.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Barrier::wait(ref<Barrier, shared> b) : bool\n    "
    "in `std::sync`\n\n    Waits until `parties` threads have called it, then lets them all go on.\n\n    `tr"
    "ue` for the last thread to arrive, the one that released the others, and `false` for the rest, so on"
    "e\n    thread of each round can do something once. A wait that fewer threads than `parties` can ever "
    "reach\n    faults (`deadlock`). A thread cancelled while it waits (`cancel`) takes its arrival back, "
    "so the round\n    still waits for `parties` threads that meet it.\n\n    Example, \"Barrier::wait: round"
    "s, one leader each\":\n        Barrier b = Barrier::new(4);\n        Atomic<u32> leaders = Atomic::new("
    "0: u32);\n        Atomic<u32> seen = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Vec<handle<void>> hs = Vec::new();\n"
    "        for (u32 i = 0; i < 4; i += 1)\n        {\n            Vec::push(&mut hs, spawn(move [](\n     "
    "           ref<Barrier, shared> b,\n                ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> leaders,\n               "
    " ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> seen,\n                u32 id,\n            )\n            {\n                "
    "for (u32 round = 0; round < 3; round += 1)\n                {\n                    _ = Atomic::fetch_a"
    "dd(seen, 1);\n                    if (Barrier::wait(b))\n                    {\n                       "
    " _ = Atomic::fetch_add(leaders, 1);\n                        assert(Atomic::load(seen) == 4 * (round "
    "+ 1));   // everyone wrote before anyone read\n                    }\n                    _ = Barrier:"
    ":wait(b);                                 // the read phase ends together too\n                }\n    "
    "        }, &b, &leaders, &seen, i));\n        }\n        foreach (h in hs)\n        {\n            join("
    "h);\n        }\n        assert(Atomic::load(&leaders) == 3 && Atomic::load(&seen) == 12);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}"
    "Semaphore\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Semaphore\u{1f}A count of permits that threads take and give back.\u{1f}\u{1f}export"
    " struct Semaphore\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A count of permits that threads take and give back.\n\n    S"
    "hared by reference, as a `mutex` is. `acquire` takes one permit, waiting while there is none; `relea"
    "se`\n    gives one back, or adds one. It bounds how many threads do something at once (connections op"
    "en, workers\n    busy); made with 0 permits, it hands events from one thread to another, each `releas"
    "e` letting one\n    `acquire` through.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::new(usize p"
    "ermits) : Semaphore\u{1f}A semaphore with `permits` permits; 0 is allowed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::new(usiz"
    "e permits) : Semaphore\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A semaphore with `permits` permits; 0 is allowed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}s"
    "td::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::acquire\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\u{1f}Takes one perm"
    "it, waiting while there is none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\n    in `std"
    "::sync`\n\n    Takes one permit, waiting while there is none.\n\n    Permits are not handed out in arriv"
    "al order. A wait no thread can end faults (`deadlock`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::try_acquire\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export"
    " fn Semaphore::try_acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) : bool\u{1f}Takes one permit if one is free, without"
    " waiting: `true` when it did.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::try_acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) : bool\n   "
    " in `std::sync`\n\n    Takes one permit if one is free, without waiting: `true` when it did.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sy"
    "nc\u{1f}Semaphore::release\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::release(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\u{1f}Gives one permit bac"
    "k, or adds one; a thread waiting in `acquire` wakes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::release(ref<Semaphore, sh"
    "ared> s)\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Gives one permit back, or adds one; a thread waiting in `acquire` w"
    "akes.\n\n    Faults (`arith_overflow`) when the permits would exceed what `usize` counts.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}"
    "Semaphore::available\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::available(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) : usize\u{1f}How many pe"
    "rmits are free now: a snapshot another thread may change at once.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::available(re"
    "f<Semaphore, shared> s) : usize\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    How many permits are free now: a snapshot an"
    "other thread may change at once.\n\n    Example, \"Semaphore: a bound and a hand-over\":\n        Semapho"
    "re limit = Semaphore::new(2);\n        Atomic<u32> active = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Atomic<u32> "
    "peak = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Vec<handle<void>> hs = Vec::new();\n        for (u32 i = 0; i < 6"
    "; i += 1)\n        {\n            Vec::push(&mut hs, spawn(move [](\n                ref<Semaphore, sha"
    "red> limit,\n                ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> active,\n                ref<Atomic<u32>, shared"
    "> peak,\n            )\n            {\n                Semaphore::acquire(limit);\n                _ = A"
    "tomic::fetch_max(peak, Atomic::fetch_add(active, 1) + 1);\n                _ = Atomic::fetch_sub(acti"
    "ve, 1);\n                Semaphore::release(limit);\n            }, &limit, &active, &peak));\n        "
    "}\n        foreach (h in hs)\n        {\n            join(h);\n        }\n        assert(Atomic::load(&pe"
    "ak) <= 2 && Semaphore::available(&limit) == 2);\n        assert(Semaphore::try_acquire(&limit) && Sem"
    "aphore::try_acquire(&limit) && !Semaphore::try_acquire(&limit));\n\n        Semaphore events = Semapho"
    "re::new(0);\n        handle<u32> h = spawn(move [](ref<Semaphore, shared> e) : u32\n        {\n        "
    "    Semaphore::acquire(e);\n            Semaphore::acquire(e);\n            Semaphore::acquire(e);\n   "
    "         3\n        }, &events);\n        Semaphore::release(&events);\n        Semaphore::release(&eve"
    "nts);\n        Semaphore::release(&events);\n        assert(join(h) == 3 && Semaphore::available(&even"
    "ts) == 0);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Once\u{1f}Something done once, by whichever thread gets "
    "there first.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Once\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Something done once, by whichever thread ge"
    "ts there first.\n\n    Shared by reference, as a `mutex` is. `Once::call(&o, f)` runs `f` the first ti"
    "me any thread calls it;\n    every other call, on any thread, returns once that run has finished, wit"
    "hout running `f`: initialising\n    what several threads share, lazily and exactly once. Should `f` f"
    "ault, the `Once` is as before, and the\n    next caller runs `f` afresh.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}exp"
    "ort fn Once::new() : Once\u{1f}A `Once` whose `f` has not run.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Once::new() : Once\n    in `std:"
    ":sync`\n\n    A `Once` whose `f` has not run.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once::call\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Once::call(ref<Once,"
    " shared> o, fn() f)\u{1f}Runs `f` if no call has run it yet; otherwise waits until the call that is runni"
    "ng it has finished.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Once::call(ref<Once, shared> o, fn() f)\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Runs "
    "`f` if no call has run it yet; otherwise waits until the call that is running it has finished.\n\n    "
    "`f` runs on the calling thread. After `call` returns, on any thread, `f` has run to its end exactly "
    "once\n    (unless it faulted, and then the next caller runs it again).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once::is_done\u{1f}fn\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn Once::is_done(ref<Once, shared> o) : bool\u{1f}Whether `f` has run to its end.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Once::"
    "is_done(ref<Once, shared> o) : bool\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Whether `f` has run to its end.\n\n    Exa"
    "mple, \"Once::call: once among four threads\":\n        Once o = Once::new();\n        Atomic<u32> runs "
    "= Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Vec<handle<bool>> hs = Vec::new();\n        for (u32 i = 0; i < 4; i +"
    "= 1)\n        {\n            Vec::push(&mut hs, spawn(move [](ref<Once, shared> o, ref<Atomic<u32>, sh"
    "ared> runs) : bool\n            {\n                Once::call(o, [runs]() { _ = Atomic::fetch_add(runs"
    ", 1); });\n                Once::is_done(o)\n            }, &o, &runs));\n        }\n        foreach (h "
    "in hs)\n        {\n            assert(join(h));\n        }\n        assert(Atomic::load(&runs) == 1 && O"
    "nce::is_done(&o));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Rng\u{1f}A general-purpose pseudo-random genera"
    "tor: xoshiro256** seeded through splitmix64.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Rng\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A general-"
    "purpose pseudo-random generator: xoshiro256** seeded through splitmix64.\n\n    The same seed gives th"
    "e same sequence in every implementation, so a run can be reproduced. Not suitable\n    for cryptograp"
    "hic purposes: its state is recoverable from its output, so it must not produce keys, tokens\n    or n"
    "onces; use `os_random_bytes` for those.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::new(u64 seed) : Rng"
    "\u{1f}A generator seeded from `seed`; equal seeds give equal sequences.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::new(u64 seed) : R"
    "ng\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A generator seeded from `seed`; equal seeds give equal sequences.\n\n    "
    "`Rng::from_os` seeds one unpredictably instead.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::next_u64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::next_u"
    "64(ref<Rng, exclusive> r) : u64\u{1f}The next 64 pseudo-random bits from `r`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::next_u64(re"
    "f<Rng, exclusive> r) : u64\n    in `std::random`\n\n    The next 64 pseudo-random bits from `r`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std:"
    ":random\u{1f}Rng::below\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::below(ref<Rng, exclusive> r, u64 n) : u64\u{1f}A pseudo-random numbe"
    "r from 0 up to, not including, `n`, each value equally likely.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::below(ref<Rng, exclus"
    "ive> r, u64 n) : u64\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A pseudo-random number from 0 up to, not including, `"
    "n`, each value equally likely.\n\n    Unbiased: a draw that would favour some values is rejected and d"
    "rawn again. Faults (`div_by_zero`) when\n    `n` is 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::unit_f64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::"
    "unit_f64(ref<Rng, exclusive> r) : f64\u{1f}A pseudo-random `f64` with `0.0 <= x < 1.0`, from the top 53 b"
    "its of one draw.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::unit_f64(ref<Rng, exclusive> r) : f64\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A p"
    "seudo-random `f64` with `0.0 <= x < 1.0`, from the top 53 bits of one draw.\n\n    Example, \"Rng: repr"
    "oducible draws in range\":\n        Rng a = Rng::new(42);\n        Rng b = Rng::new(42);\n        assert"
    "(Rng::next_u64(&mut a) == Rng::next_u64(&mut b));\n        for (usize i = 0; i < 100; i += 1)\n       "
    " {\n            assert(Rng::below(&mut a, 6) < 6);\n            f64 x = Rng::unit_f64(&mut a);\n       "
    "     assert(x >= 0.0 && x < 1.0);\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}os_random_bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn os_random_byt"
    "es(slice<u8, exclusive> out)\u{1f}Fills `out` with bytes from the operating system's cryptographically se"
    "cure source.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn os_random_bytes(slice<u8, exclusive> out)\n    in `std::random`\n\n    Fills `o"
    "ut` with bytes from the operating system's cryptographically secure source.\n\n    Suitable for keys, "
    "tokens and nonces, and for seeding `Rng`. Faults (`entropy_unavailable`) when the\n    system has no "
    "such source.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}os_random_u64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn os_random_u64() : u64\u{1f}A `u64` from the operati"
    "ng system's cryptographically secure source.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn os_random_u64() : u64\n    in `std::random`\n\n"
    "    A `u64` from the operating system's cryptographically secure source.\n\n    Faults (`entropy_unava"
    "ilable`) when the system has no such source.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::from_os\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rng::from_os() "
    ": Rng\u{1f}A generator seeded from the operating system's secure source, so each run draws a different se"
    "quence.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::from_os() : Rng\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A generator seeded from the operat"
    "ing system's secure source, so each run draws a different sequence.\n\n    The sequence itself is stil"
    "l `Rng`'s, so it is still not for cryptographic purposes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}Rng::shuffle\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Rn"
    "g::shuffle<T>(ref<Rng, exclusive> r, slice<T, exclusive> s)\u{1f}Puts the elements of `s` in a uniformly "
    "random order drawn from `r`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Rng::shuffle<T>(ref<Rng, exclusive> r, slice<T, exclusive> s"
    ")\n    in `std::random`\n\n    Puts the elements of `s` in a uniformly random order drawn from `r`.\n\n  "
    "  Fisher-Yates over `Rng::below`; elements are exchanged, never copied. The same seed gives the same"
    " order\n    in every implementation.\n\n    Example, \"Rng::shuffle: a Vec through its slice\":\n        R"
    "ng r = Rng::new(7);\n        Vec<i32> v = Vec::new();\n        for (i32 i = 1; i <= 5; i += 1)\n       "
    " {\n            Vec::push(&mut v, i);\n        }\n        Rng::shuffle(&mut r, &mut v);\n        assert("
    "Vec::len(&v) == 5 && Vec::contains(&v, 3));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::random\u{1f}uuid_v4\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn uuid_v4() : String\u{1f}A "
    "version 4 UUID (RFC 9562) from the operating system's secure source, as 36 lowercase characters.\u{1f}\u{1f}ex"
    "port fn uuid_v4() : String\n    in `std::random`\n\n    A version 4 UUID (RFC 9562) from the operating "
    "system's secure source, as 36 lowercase characters.\n\n    The form is `xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxx"
    "xxxxxx`, with `y` one of `8`, `9`, `a`, `b`. Faults\n    (`entropy_unavailable`) when the system has "
    "no secure source.\n\n    Example, \"uuid_v4: the shape of the text\":\n        String id = uuid_v4();\n   "
    "     assert(StringView::len(&id) == 36);\n        assert(&id[8..9] == \"-\");\n        assert(&id[14..15"
    "] == \"4\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}min\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn min<T: ordered>(T a, T b) : T\u{1f}The smaller of `a` and `b`; `a"
    "` when they are equal.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn min<T: ordered>(T a, T b) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The smaller "
    "of `a` and `b`; `a` when they are equal.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}max\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn max<T: ordered>(T a, T b) : T\u{1f}"
    "The larger of `a` and `b`; `a` when they are equal.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn max<T: ordered>(T a, T b) : T\n    in "
    "`std::math`\n\n    The larger of `a` and `b`; `a` when they are equal.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}abs\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ab"
    "s<T: number>(T x) : T\u{1f}The magnitude of `x`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn abs<T: number>(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n "
    "   The magnitude of `x`.\n\n    Checked: faults (`arith_overflow`) for a signed type's minimum, whose "
    "magnitude does not fit. `abs(-0.0)`\n    is `0.0`, and a NaN stays a NaN.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}pow\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export f"
    "n pow<T: number>(T base, u32 exp) : T\u{1f}`base` raised to the power `exp`, by repeated squaring; `pow(x"
    ", 0)` is 1.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn pow<T: number>(T base, u32 exp) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `base` raised to "
    "the power `exp`, by repeated squaring; `pow(x, 0)` is 1.\n\n    For an integer type the result is exac"
    "t, and checked: faults (`arith_overflow`) only when it does not\n    fit in `T`. For a float base eac"
    "h multiplication rounds, so a large `exp` can be off by several units in\n    the last place (`pow(1."
    "01, 500)`); `powf` is within one unit, and takes a floating-point exponent.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}clamp\u{1f}fn\u{1f}exp"
    "ort fn clamp<T: ordered>(T x, T lo, T hi) : T\u{1f}`x` held within `lo ..= hi`: `lo` when `x` is below it"
    ", `hi` when above, else `x`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn clamp<T: ordered>(T x, T lo, T hi) : T\n    in `std::math`\n  "
    "  requires\n        !(hi < lo), assert_failed, \"clamp: `lo` is above `hi`\"\n\n    `x` held within `lo ."
    ".= hi`: `lo` when `x` is below it, `hi` when above, else `x`.\n\n    Faults (`assert_failed`) when `lo"
    "` is above `hi`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}is_nan\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn is_nan<T: number>(T x) : bool\u{1f}Whether `x` is a NaN,"
    " the one value not equal to itself; `false` for every integer.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn is_nan<T: number>(T x) : b"
    "ool\n    in `std::math`\n\n    Whether `x` is a NaN, the one value not equal to itself; `false` for eve"
    "ry integer.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}is_finite\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn is_finite<T: number>(T x) : bool\u{1f}Whether `x` is neith"
    "er a NaN nor an infinity; `true` for every integer.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn is_finite<T: number>(T x) : bool\n    "
    "in `std::math`\n\n    Whether `x` is neither a NaN nor an infinity; `true` for every integer.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::m"
    "ath\u{1f}gcd\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn gcd<T: integer>(T a, T b) : T\u{1f}The greatest common divisor of `a` and `b`, never"
    " negative; `gcd(0, 0)` is 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn gcd<T: integer>(T a, T b) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The gr"
    "eatest common divisor of `a` and `b`, never negative; `gcd(0, 0)` is 0.\n\n    Euclid's algorithm over"
    " the magnitudes, so a signed type's minimum faults (`arith_overflow`) as in `abs`.\n\n    Example, \"gc"
    "d: with clamp, pow, abs and the float tests\":\n        assert(gcd(-12, 18) == 6);\n        assert(gcd("
    "0, 0) == 0);\n        assert(clamp(15, 0, 10) == 10 && clamp(-3, 0, 10) == 0);\n        assert(pow(3, "
    "4) == 81 && pow(7, 0) == 1);\n        assert(abs(-0.0) == 0.0 && is_nan(0.0 / 0.0) && !is_finite(1.0 "
    "/ 0.0));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}BigUint\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct BigUint\u{1f}An unsigned integer of any size, for publi"
    "c-key arithmetic and numbers too large for `u128`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct BigUint\n    in `std::math`\n\n    An"
    " unsigned integer of any size, for public-key arithmetic and numbers too large for `u128`.\n\n    Each"
    " operation gives the exact integer result. The time an operation takes depends on its operands'\n    "
    "values, so a `BigUint` is for public values only, never a private key or anything secret. It owns it"
    "s\n    digits, so a program reassigns one with `overwrite`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}BigUint::zero\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Bi"
    "gUint::zero() : BigUint\u{1f}The number 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn BigUint::zero() : BigUint\n    in `std::math`\n\n    T"
    "he number 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}BigUint::from_u64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn BigUint::from_u64(u64 x) : BigUint\u{1f}The numbe"
    "r `x`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn BigUint::from_u64(u64 x) : BigUint\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The number `x`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "math\u{1f}BigUint::from_bytes_be\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn BigUint::from_bytes_be(slice<u8, shared> bytes) : BigUint\u{1f}T"
    "he number whose big-endian bytes are `bytes`; leading zero bytes are allowed, and no bytes give 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "export fn BigUint::from_bytes_be(slice<u8, shared> bytes) : BigUint\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The numb"
    "er whose big-endian bytes are `bytes`; leading zero bytes are allowed, and no bytes give 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::m"
    "ath\u{1f}BigUint::to_bytes_be\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn BigUint::to_bytes_be(ref<BigUint, shared> a) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}The big"
    "-endian bytes of `a`, with no leading zero byte; none for zero.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn BigUint::to_bytes_be(ref<"
    "BigUint, shared> a) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The big-endian bytes of `a`, with no leading z"
