    "ared> a, ref<BigUint, shared> m) : Option<BigUint>\u{1f}The inverse of `a` modulo `m`: the number below `"
    "m` whose product with `a` is 1 modulo `m`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn BigUint::mod_inverse(ref<BigUint, shared> a, r"
    "ef<BigUint, shared> m) : Option<BigUint>\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The inverse of `a` modulo `m`: the "
    "number below `m` whose product with `a` is 1 modulo `m`.\n\n    `None` when `a` and `m` share a factor"
    " above 1, or when `m` is below 2. Its time depends on the values,\n    as every `BigUint` operation's"
    " does: for public numbers and one-time blinding factors, not a private key.\n\n    Example, \"BigUint::"
    "mod_inverse: with and without an inverse\":\n        BigUint m = BigUint::from_u64(11);\n        match "
    "(BigUint::mod_inverse(&BigUint::from_u64(3), &m))\n        {\n            Some(x) : assert(BigUint::eq"
    "(&x, &BigUint::from_u64(4))),\n            None    : assert(false),\n        }\n        assert(Option::"
    "is_none(&BigUint::mod_inverse(&BigUint::from_u64(6), &BigUint::from_u64(9))));\n        BigUint p = B"
    "igUint::mod_pow(&BigUint::from_u64(3), &BigUint::from_u64(10), &m);\n        assert(BigUint::eq(&p, &"
    "BigUint::from_u64(1)));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}BigUint::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn BigUint::text(ref<BigUint, shared> a)"
    " : String\u{1f}`a` in decimal digits, with no leading zero.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn BigUint::text(ref<BigUint, shared>"
    " a) : String\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `a` in decimal digits, with no leading zero.\n\n    Example, \"Big"
    "Uint::text: past u64 and back\":\n        BigUint big = BigUint::shift_left(&BigUint::from_u64(1), 100"
