    "tandard output, moved out of the `Child` with whatever was read ahead.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Child::take_output"
    "(ref<Child, exclusive> ch) : Option<ChildOutput>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    The child's standard out"
    "put, moved out of the `Child` with whatever was read ahead.\n\n    `Child::read_output` then finds the"
    " end. `None` when the output was taken already.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildInput::write\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ChildI"
    "nput::write(ref<ChildInput, exclusive> p, slice<u8, shared> data) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Writes a"
    "ll of `data` to the child's standard input, as `Child::write_input` does.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ChildInput::wri"
    "te(ref<ChildInput, exclusive> p, slice<u8, shared> data) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::proc"
    "ess`\n\n    Writes all of `data` to the child's standard input, as `Child::write_input` does.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::p"
    "rocess\u{1f}ChildInput::drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ChildInput::drop(ref<ChildInput, exclusive> self)\u{1f}Closes the pi"
    "pe when its `ChildInput` is destroyed, so the child reads the end of its input.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ChildInpu"
    "t::drop(ref<ChildInput, exclusive> self)\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Closes the pipe when its `ChildI"
    "nput` is destroyed, so the child reads the end of its input.\n\n    The destructor; programs do not ca"
    "ll it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildOutput::read\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput::read(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> p"
    ", ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf, usize max) : Result<usize, FileError>\u{1f}Appends to `buf` what has arriv"
    "ed on the child's standard output, up to `max` bytes, and returns how many.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput::"
    "read(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> p, ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf, usize max) : Result<usize, FileErro"
    "r>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Appends to `buf` what has arrived on the child's standard output, up t"
    "o `max` bytes, and returns how many.\n\n    As `Child::read_output`: at most a MiB at a time, and `Ok("
    "0)` (for a `max` above 0) only at the end.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}ChildOutput::read_line\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ChildO"
    "utput::read_line(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> p) : Result<Option<String>, FileError>\u{1f}The next line of"
    " the child's standard output, as `Child::read_output_line` reads it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput::read_li"
    "ne(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> p) : Result<Option<String>, FileError>\n    in `std::process`\n\n    The"
    " next line of the child's standard output, as `Child::read_output_line` reads it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}Chi"
    "ldOutput::drop\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput::drop(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> self)\u{1f}Closes the pipe when"
    " its `ChildOutput` is destroyed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn ChildOutput::drop(ref<ChildOutput, exclusive> self)\n    "
    "in `std::process`\n\n    Closes the pipe when its `ChildOutput` is destroyed.\n\n    The destructor; pro"
    "grams do not call it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}process_id\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn process_id() : u64\u{1f}The operating system"
    "'s number for this program (its process id), as a pid file records it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn process_id() : u64"
    "\n    in `std::process`\n\n    The operating system's number for this program (its process id), as a pi"
    "d file records it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}watch_interrupts\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn watch_interrupts()\u{1f}From now on, make"
    "s an interrupt set the flag `interrupt_requested` reads instead of ending the program.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn wa"
    "tch_interrupts()\n    in `std::process`\n\n    From now on, makes an interrupt set the flag `interrupt_"
    "requested` reads instead of ending the program.\n\n    An interrupt is SIGINT or SIGTERM on Unix; Ctrl"
    "-C, Ctrl-Break or closing the console on Windows. A\n    blocking socket call returns early on an int"
    "errupt the program has not seen yet, one that arrives while\n    it waits or since the program last c"
    "alled `interrupt_requested` (`accept` and a socket's `read` give\n    `Err(TimedOut)`), so a long-run"
    "ning loop checks the flag and stops cleanly. Once the program has seen\n    the flag set, its later c"
    "alls wait as usual, so a clean shutdown can finish its exchanges, until\n    another interrupt arrive"
    "s. A socket call already waiting when an interrupt arrives returns early even\n    if another thread "
