    "rgon2id prescribes; that addressing is outside `std::crypto`'s constant-time guarantee.\n\n    Faults "
    "(`kdf_parameters`) when `iterations` is 0, `parallelism` is 0 or above 255, `memory_kib` is below 8\n"
    "    × `parallelism`, `salt` is shorter than 8 bytes or `len` is below 4, or when `iterations`, `mem"
    "ory_kib`\n    or `len` is above 2^32 − 1 (RFC 9106's bounds).\n\n    Cost: time grows with `iteration"
    "s` × `memory_kib`, and `memory_kib` KiB are allocated. To store a\n    password, `hash_password` cho"
    "oses the parameters.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::crypto::kdf\u{1f}hash_password\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn hash_password(slice<u8, shared> p"
    "assword) : String\u{1f}`password` hashed for storage: an Argon2id PHC string with a fresh random salt.\u{1f}\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn hash_password(slice<u8, shared> password) : String\n    in `std::crypto::kdf`\n\n    `password"
    "` hashed for storage: an Argon2id PHC string with a fresh random salt.\n\n    The text `$argon2id$v=19"
    "$m=19456,t=2,p=1$S$H`, S the unpadded base64 of 16 bytes of `os_random_bytes` and\n    H that of `arg"
    "on2id(password, salt, 2, 19456, 1, 32)`: 19 MiB, two passes and one lane, the OWASP\n    recommendati"
    "on. `verify_password` and every password library read it.\n\n    Slow by design, so that guessing stay"
    "s expensive.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::crypto::kdf\u{1f}verify_password\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn verify_password(StringView stored, slic"
    "e<u8, shared> password) : bool\u{1f}Whether `password` is the one the Argon2id PHC string `stored` was ma"
    "de from.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn verify_password(StringView stored, slice<u8, shared> password) : bool\n    in `st"
    "d::crypto::kdf`\n\n    Whether `password` is the one the Argon2id PHC string `stored` was made from.\n\n"
    "    `stored` is a hash written by `hash_password` or by any Argon2id implementation\n    (`$argon2id$"
    "v=19$m=M,t=T,p=P$salt$hash`); its parameters are taken from it, and the result is compared\n    with "
    "`digest_eq`. `false` when `stored` does not have that shape, its parameters are outside the bounds\n "
    "   `argon2id` accepts (so it never faults on them), or its memory `m` is above 1,048,576 KiB (1 GiB,"
    "\n    libsodium's largest preset), so a hostile stored hash cannot make one call allocate more. Cost:"
    " one\n    `argon2id` with the stored parameters.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::crypto::aead\u{1f}chacha20\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn chacha20(s"
