    "re::system\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::system() : Result<TrustStore, FileError>\u{1f}The operating system's "
    "roots, from the first of the usual bundle files that holds a certificate.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::sys"
    "tem() : Result<TrustStore, FileError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The operating system's roots, from the"
    " first of the usual bundle files that holds a certificate.\n\n    The files tried, in order: `/etc/ssl"
    "/certs/ca-certificates.crt` (Debian, Ubuntu),\n    `/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt` (Fedora, RHEL),"
    " `/etc/ssl/ca-bundle.pem`, `/etc/ssl/cert.pem` (Alpine)\n    and `/usr/local/etc/openssl/cert.pem` (m"
    "acOS with a package manager's OpenSSL). `Err(NotFound)` where none\n    does, as on Windows: a progra"
    "m there passes a bundle to `TrustStore::from_pem_file`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}verify_signature\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn ve"
    "rify_signature(ref<CertKey, shared> key, ref<SignatureScheme, shared> scheme, slice<u8, shared> mess"
    "age, slice<u8, shared> signature) : bool\u{1f}Whether `signature` over `message` verifies under `key` wit"
