    "t constant-time, and need not be: it uses public values only.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}Certificate::matches_host\u{1f}"
    "fn\u{1f}export fn Certificate::matches_host(ref<Certificate, shared> c, StringView host) : bool\u{1f}Whether `"
    "c` is for `host` (RFC 6125 §6.4).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Certificate::matches_host(ref<Certificate, shared> c, "
    "StringView host) : bool\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Whether `c` is for `host` (RFC 6125 §6.4).\n\n    An "
    "IP address literal is compared with the certificate's IP addresses. A name is compared with its DNS\n"
    "    names, ignoring ASCII case and one final dot on `host`; a leading `*.` in a DNS name stands for "
    "exactly\n    one whole label, and only where at least two labels follow it (so `*.com` matches nothin"
    "g). The common\n    name is not consulted.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}verify_chain\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn verify_chain(ref<Cer"
