    "ingView host, ref<DateTime, shared> now) : Result<void, CertError>\u{1f}Verifies a TLS server's certifica"
    "te chain from `leaf` to one of `roots`, for `host` at the time `now`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn verify_chain(ref<Ce"
    "rtificate, shared> leaf, slice<Certificate, shared> intermediates, ref<TrustStore, shared> roots, St"
    "ringView host, ref<DateTime, shared> now) : Result<void, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Verifies"
    " a TLS server's certificate chain from `leaf` to one of `roots`, for `host` at the time `now`.\n\n    "
    "`Ok(())` when the leaf matches `host` (`Certificate::matches_host`), may serve TLS, is in date and u"
    "sable,\n    and a chain of at most 10 certificates below the root exists (RFC 5280 §6, as a client n"
    "eeds it) in\n    which:\n\n    - each certificate is signed by the next, found by issuer name and signa"
    "ture among `intermediates`, in any\n      order, or among the roots;\n    - every issuer, the root inc"
    "luded, is a CA allowed to sign certificates, allowed by its extended key usage\n      (when it has on"
    "e) to serve TLS servers, in date and usable, and within its path length;\n    - every DNS name and IP"
    " address of each certificate below an issuer, and `host`, is within the issuer's\n      name constrai"
    "nts (its permitted and excluded `dNSName` and `iPAddress` subtrees, a wildcard name read\n      as wr"
    "itten; a critical name constraint of another form makes the issuer `UnhandledCritical`);\n    - the l"
    "ast is one of the roots.\n\n    When several certificates could issue the same one (an expired and a r"
    "enewed intermediate, a cross\n    sign), each is tried in turn until a chain verifies, within 100 sig"
    "nature checks in all.\n\n    Otherwise `Err`: `HostMismatch`, then `WrongUsage`, then `NotYetValid`, `"
    "Expired` or `UnhandledCritical`\n    for the leaf; then the reason the last candidate issuer tried fa"
    "iled (`UnknownAuthority` when there was\n    none, `BadSignature`, `NotAuthority` for an issuer that "
    "is not a CA, is beyond its path length or whose\n    name constraints exclude a name, `WrongUsage`, `"
    "NotYetValid`, `Expired`, `UnhandledCritical` or\n    `ChainTooLong`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertKey::to_der\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn CertKey::to_der(ref<CertKey, shared> key) : Option<Vec<u8>>\u{1f}The DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo o"
    "f `key`, or `None` for `UnsupportedKey`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CertKey::to_der(ref<CertKey, shared> key) : Opti"
