    "ringView text) : Result<CertKey, CertError>\u{1f}The public key of the first `-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----`"
    " block in `text` (RFC 7468).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CertKey::from_pem(StringView text) : Result<CertKey, CertErr"
    "or>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The public key of the first `-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----` block in `text`"
    " (RFC 7468).\n\n    The block's DER is read as `CertKey::from_der` reads it; `Err(BadEncoding)` when t"
    "here is no such block,\n    or its base64 does not decode.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertKey::to_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn C"
    "ertKey::to_pem(ref<CertKey, shared> key) : Option<String>\u{1f}`key` as a PEM `PUBLIC KEY` block of 64-ch"
    "aracter lines, or `None` for `UnsupportedKey`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CertKey::to_pem(ref<CertKey, shared> key) "
    ": Option<String>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    `key` as a PEM `PUBLIC KEY` block of 64-character lines, or"
    " `None` for `UnsupportedKey`.\n\n    Example, \"CertKey::to_pem: read back by from_pem\":\n        CertKe"
    "y key = Ed25519Key([0x42; 32]);\n        String pem = Option::unwrap(CertKey::to_pem(&key));\n        "
    "assert(StringView::starts_with(&pem, \"-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\\n\"));\n        match (CertKey::from_"
    "pem(&pem))\n        {\n            Ok(Ed25519Key(k)) : assert(k[0] == 0x42 && k[31] == 0x42),\n        "
    "    _                 : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}EcPrivateKey\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct EcPri"
    "vateKey\u{1f}An elliptic-curve private key: the curve and the scalar, 32 bytes for P-256 or 48 for P-384."
    "\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct EcPrivateKey\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    An elliptic-curve private key: the curve and th"
    "e scalar, 32 bytes for P-256 or 48 for P-384.\n\n    Fields:\n        EcCurve curve\n        Vec<u8> sca"
    "lar\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}PrivateKey\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum PrivateKey\u{1f}A private key of one of the algorithms `std` "
    "signs with.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum PrivateKey\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    A private key of one of the algorithms `"
    "std` signs with.\n\n    - `RsaPrivate`: an RSA key.\n    - `EcPrivate`: a P-256 or P-384 key.\n    - `Ed"
    "25519Private`: an Ed25519 key, its 32-byte private key (the seed).\n\n    Variants:\n        RsaPrivate"
    "(RsaPrivateKey)\n        EcPrivate(EcPrivateKey)\n        Ed25519Private(array<u8, 32>)\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}Pr"
    "ivateKey::public_key\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::public_key(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key) : CertKey\u{1f}The "
    "public key that matches `key`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::public_key(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key) : Cert"
    "Key\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The public key that matches `key`.\n\n    An EC key whose scalar does not "
    "name a number in [1, n-1], which `PrivateKey::from_der` never gives, gets\n    an empty point; a scal"
    "ar of the wrong length faults (`crypto_length`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}PrivateKey::from_der\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Priva"
    "teKey::from_der(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result<PrivateKey, CertError>\u{1f}The private key of the DER `d"
    "er`: a PKCS #8 PrivateKeyInfo (RFC 5958), PKCS #1 RSAPrivateKey or SEC 1 ECPrivateKey.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Pr"
    "ivateKey::from_der(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result<PrivateKey, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Th"
    "e private key of the DER `der`: a PKCS #8 PrivateKeyInfo (RFC 5958), PKCS #1 RSAPrivateKey or SEC 1\n"
    "    ECPrivateKey.\n\n    The three are told apart by their first fields; a SEC 1 key's curve comes fro"
    "m its own parameters. The\n    numbers are checked as `RsaPrivateKey::new` and `ec_public_key` check "
    "them. `Err(BadEncoding)` when `der`\n    is none of these or its numbers do not fit together; `Err(Un"
    "supportedAlgorithm)` for an algorithm or curve\n    `std` does not sign with.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}PrivateKey:"
    ":to_der\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::to_der(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}`key` as DER PKCS #8 "
    "(version 0), which `PrivateKey::from_der` reads back.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::to_der(ref<PrivateKey, "
    "shared> key) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    `key` as DER PKCS #8 (version 0), which `PrivateKey::"
    "from_der` reads back.\n\n    An RSA key with its Chinese-remainder values, an EC key with its public k"
    "ey, an Ed25519 key as its seed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}PrivateKey::from_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::from_pem(S"
    "tringView text) : Result<PrivateKey, CertError>\u{1f}The private key of a `PRIVATE KEY`, `RSA PRIVATE KEY"
    "` or `EC PRIVATE KEY` block in `text`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::from_pem(StringView text) : Result<Pri"
    "vateKey, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The private key of a `PRIVATE KEY`, `RSA PRIVATE KEY` or"
    " `EC PRIVATE KEY` block in `text`.\n\n    The block's DER is read as `PrivateKey::from_der` reads it. "
    "The labels are looked for in that order, so a\n    `PRIVATE KEY` block is taken even when a block of "
    "the other kinds comes before it. An\n    `ENCRYPTED PRIVATE KEY` block alone is `Err(UnsupportedAlgor"
    "ithm)`; no block, or base64 that does not\n    decode, is `Err(BadEncoding)`.\n\n    Example, \"PrivateK"
    "ey::from_pem: an encrypted key is not read\":\n        StringView text = \"-----BEGIN ENCRYPTED PRIVATE"
    " KEY-----\\nAAAA\\n-----END ENCRYPTED PRIVATE KEY-----\\n\";\n        match (PrivateKey::from_pem(text))\n"
    "        {\n            Err(UnsupportedAlgorithm) : assert(true),\n            _                       "
    "  : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}PrivateKey::to_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::to_pem(ref<Priv"
    "ateKey, shared> key) : String\u{1f}`key` as a PEM `PRIVATE KEY` block (PKCS #8) of 64-character lines.\u{1f}\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn PrivateKey::to_pem(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key) : String\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    `key` as a"
    " PEM `PRIVATE KEY` block (PKCS #8) of 64-character lines.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}sign\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn sign(ref<Pri"
    "vateKey, shared> key, ref<SignatureScheme, shared> scheme, slice<u8, shared> message) : Option<Vec<u"
    "8>>\u{1f}`key`'s signature of `message` under `scheme`, which `verify_signature` accepts with the matchin"
    "g public key.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn sign(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key, ref<SignatureScheme, shared> scheme, slic"
    "e<u8, shared> message) : Option<Vec<u8>>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    `key`'s signature of `message` unde"
    "r `scheme`, which `verify_signature` accepts with the matching public\n    key.\n\n    The RSA PKCS #1 "
    "v1.5, RSA-PSS and ECDSA schemes sign the scheme's hash of `message`; Ed25519 signs\n    `message` who"
    "le. `None` when `key` is not of the scheme's kind, the scheme is `UnsupportedSignature`, or\n    an E"
    "C key's scalar is not in [1, n-1]. An RSA modulus too short for the scheme's hash faults\n    (`crypt"
    "o_length`).\n\n    Example, \"sign: a key of another kind gives None\":\n        PrivateKey key = Ed25519"
    "Private([1; 32]);\n        SignatureScheme scheme = RsaPss(Sha2_256);\n        assert(Option::is_none("
    "&sign(&key, &scheme, b\"message\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum TlsError\u{1f}Why a TLS connecti"
    "on failed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum TlsError\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Why a TLS connection failed.\n\n    - `TlsNetF"
    "ailure(e)`: the socket failed as `e` says; also a line `read_line` read that is not UTF-8\n      (`No"
    "tUtf8`), and a `read_exact` cut short (`Closed`).\n    - `CertRejected(e)`: the server's certificate "
    "chain did not verify, as `e` says.\n    - `HandshakeFailed`: a negotiation this side cannot complete."
    "\n    - `ProtocolError`: the peer sent a malformed message.\n    - `PeerAlert(code)`: the peer sent an"
    " alert with this description code (40 handshake_failure, 70\n      protocol_version, and so on).\n    "
    "- `RecordRejected`: a record did not authenticate.\n\n    Variants:\n        TlsNetFailure(NetError)\n  "
    "      CertRejected(CertError)\n        HandshakeFailed\n        ProtocolError\n        PeerAlert(u8)\n  "
    "      RecordRejected\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsError::text(ref<TlsError, shared> e) "
    ": str\u{1f}A one-line description of the error, for messages; the common alert codes are named.\u{1f}\u{1f}export f"
    "n TlsError::text(ref<TlsError, shared> e) : str\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    A one-line description of the"
    " error, for messages; the common alert codes are named.\n\n    Example, \"TlsError::text: alerts and ne"
    "twork failures\":\n        TlsError e = PeerAlert(70);\n        assert(TlsError::text(&e) == \"the peer "
    "does not speak TLS 1.3 (alert 70)\");\n        TlsError n = TlsNetFailure(Refused);\n        assert(Tls"
    "Error::text(&n) == \"connection refused\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct TlsStre"
    "am\u{1f}A TLS 1.3 connection over a `TcpStream`, as a client (`client`, `connect`) or as a server (`serve"
    "r`).\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct TlsStream\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    A TLS 1.3 connection over a `TcpStream"
    "`, as a client (`client`, `connect`) or as a server (`server`).\n\n    It speaks the cipher suites TLS"
    "_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256, TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 and\n    TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384, the key exchanges "
    "X25519, P-256 and P-384, and ECDSA, RSA-PSS and Ed25519\n    signatures. No TLS 1.2, no session resum"
    "ption, no early data, no client certificates: a client asked\n    for one answers with none, as RFC 8"
    "446 §4.4.2 allows, and a server that requires one then refuses\n    with alert 116 (`PeerAlert(116)`"
    "). Dropping the stream closes the connection without close_notify; `close` sends it first.\n\n    Impl"
    "emented to RFC 8446, tested against its vectors and against OpenSSL on loopback, and fuzzed\n    cont"
    "inuously; not independently audited.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::peer_certificate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::"
    "peer_certificate(ref<TlsStream, shared> s) : Option<ref<Certificate, shared>>\u{1f}The peer's certificate"
    " that the handshake verified: on a client's stream, the server's leaf.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::peer_ce"
    "rtificate(ref<TlsStream, shared> s) : Option<ref<Certificate, shared>>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    The pe"
    "er's certificate that the handshake verified: on a client's stream, the server's leaf.\n\n    `None` o"
    "n a server's stream, since clients send none. A program that pins a key or a certificate\n    compare"
    "s it here.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::peer_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::peer_addr(ref<TlsStream, shared> "
    "s) : SocketAddr\u{1f}The address of the other end of the connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::peer_addr(ref<"
    "TlsStream, shared> s) : SocketAddr\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    The address of the other end of the connec"
    "tion.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::local_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::local_addr(ref<TlsStream, shared> s) "
    ": SocketAddr\u{1f}The local address of the connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::local_addr(ref<TlsStream, sh"
    "ared> s) : SocketAddr\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    The local address of the connection.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStre"
    "am::set_read_timeout_ms\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::set_read_timeout_ms(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s, u64"
    " ms)\u{1f}Sets how long a read waits for data, in milliseconds, as `TcpStream::set_read_timeout_ms` does "
    "on the stream's socket; 0 waits for ever.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::set_read_timeout_ms(ref<TlsStream, e"
    "xclusive> s, u64 ms)\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Sets how long a read waits for data, in milliseconds, as"
    " `TcpStream::set_read_timeout_ms` does on the\n    stream's socket; 0 waits for ever.\n\n    A read tha"
    "t times out between records leaves the stream usable; one that times out inside a record\n    leaves "
    "it unusable (the next record does not authenticate, `Err(RecordRejected)`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::se"
    "t_write_timeout_ms\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::set_write_timeout_ms(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s, u64 ms)"
    "\u{1f}Sets how long a write waits, in milliseconds, as `TcpStream::set_write_timeout_ms` does on the stre"
    "am's socket; 0 waits for ever.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::set_write_timeout_ms(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> "
    "s, u64 ms)\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Sets how long a write waits, in milliseconds, as `TcpStream::set_w"
    "rite_timeout_ms` does on the stream's\n    socket; 0 waits for ever.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::client\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn TlsStream::client(TcpStream tcp, StringView server_name, ref<TrustStore, shared> roots) : "
    "Result<TlsStream, TlsError>\u{1f}Performs the TLS 1.3 handshake as a client over the connected `tcp`, and"
    " gives the stream.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::client(TcpStream tcp, StringView server_name, ref<TrustStor"
    "e, shared> roots) : Result<TlsStream, TlsError>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Performs the TLS 1.3 handshak"
    "e as a client over the connected `tcp`, and gives the stream.\n\n    `server_name` is a DNS name, sent"
    " as SNI and checked against the certificate, or an IP address\n    literal, checked against its IP ad"
    "dresses. The server's chain is verified against `roots` at the\n    current time. The timeouts set on"
    " `tcp` apply to every read and write. `Err(CertRejected(e))` for a\n    chain that does not verify, `"
    "Err(HandshakeFailed)` for a negotiation this client cannot complete,\n    `Err(PeerAlert(code))` when"
    " the server refuses.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::connect\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::connect(SocketAddr addr, "
    "StringView server_name, ref<TrustStore, shared> roots) : Result<TlsStream, TlsError>\u{1f}Connects to `ad"
    "dr` with `TcpStream::connect` and performs the handshake as `client` does.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::con"
    "nect(SocketAddr addr, StringView server_name, ref<TrustStore, shared> roots) : Result<TlsStream, Tls"
    "Error>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Connects to `addr` with `TcpStream::connect` and performs the handshak"
    "e as `client` does.\n\n    A failure to connect is `Err(TlsNetFailure(e))`. For a bounded wait, connec"
    "t with\n    `TcpStream::connect_timeout` and call `client`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::write\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn "
    "TlsStream::write(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s, slice<u8, shared> data) : Result<void, TlsError>\u{1f}Sends"
    " all of `data`, encrypted, in records of at most 16 KiB.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::write(ref<TlsStream, "
    "exclusive> s, slice<u8, shared> data) : Result<void, TlsError>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Sends all of `"
    "data`, encrypted, in records of at most 16 KiB.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::write_text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStr"
    "eam::write_text(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s, StringView text) : Result<void, TlsError>\u{1f}Sends the byt"
    "es of `text`, as `write` does.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::write_text(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s, StringV"
    "iew text) : Result<void, TlsError>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Sends the bytes of `text`, as `write` does"
    ".\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::read\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::read(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s, ref<Vec<u8>, "
    "exclusive> buf, usize max) : Result<usize, TlsError>\u{1f}Appends up to `max` bytes of the peer's data to"
    " `buf`, waiting for some, and gives how many.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::read(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s"
    ", ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf, usize max) : Result<usize, TlsError>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Appends u"
    "p to `max` bytes of the peer's data to `buf`, waiting for some, and gives how many.\n\n    0 when the "
    "peer has closed the connection with close_notify (or when `max` is 0). Key updates and\n    session t"
    "ickets the peer sends are handled on the way. `Err(RecordRejected)` for a record that does not\n    a"
    "uthenticate, `Err(PeerAlert(code))` for an alert.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::read_exact\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsS"
    "tream::read_exact(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s, ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf, usize n) : Result<void, "
    "TlsError>\u{1f}Appends exactly `n` bytes of the peer's data to `buf`, reading until they have all arrived"
    ".\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::read_exact(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s, ref<Vec<u8>, exclusive> buf, usize n"
    ") : Result<void, TlsError>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Appends exactly `n` bytes of the peer's data to `b"
    "uf`, reading until they have all arrived.\n\n    `Err(TlsNetFailure(Closed))` when the peer closes fir"
    "st; what arrived before that stays in `buf`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::read_line\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream:"
    ":read_line(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s) : Result<Option<String>, TlsError>\u{1f}The next line the peer se"
    "nt, without its `\\n` (nor a `\\r` before it).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::read_line(ref<TlsStream, exclusiv"
    "e> s) : Result<Option<String>, TlsError>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    The next line the peer sent, without"
    " its `\\n` (nor a `\\r` before it).\n\n    `Ok(None)` when the peer has closed (close_notify) before any"
    " byte; a last line without `\\n` is given\n    as it is. `Err(TlsNetFailure(NotUtf8(e)))` for a line t"
    "hat is not UTF-8.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::close\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::close(ref<TlsStream, exclusive"
    "> s) : Result<void, TlsError>\u{1f}Sends close_notify, telling the peer that no more data follows.\u{1f}\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn TlsStream::close(ref<TlsStream, exclusive> s) : Result<void, TlsError>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    S"
    "ends close_notify, telling the peer that no more data follows.\n\n    The peer may still send what it "
    "had in flight, and `read` still reads it. Dropping a `TlsStream`\n    without `close` just closes the"
    " connection.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::server\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::server(TcpStream tcp, ref<PrivateK"
    "ey, shared> key, slice<Certificate, shared> chain) : Result<TlsStream, TlsError>\u{1f}Performs the TLS 1."
    "3 handshake as a server over the accepted `tcp`, and gives the stream.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::server("
    "TcpStream tcp, ref<PrivateKey, shared> key, slice<Certificate, shared> chain) : Result<TlsStream, Tl"
    "sError>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Performs the TLS 1.3 handshake as a server over the accepted `tcp`, a"
    "nd gives the stream.\n\n    `key` is the server's private key and `chain` its certificate first, then "
    "its issuers up to, but not\n    including, the root. The suite and the group are chosen in the client"
    "'s order of preference. A\n    client that does not speak TLS 1.3, or offers no suite, group or signa"
    "ture scheme in common, is\n    sent an alert and the result is `Err(HandshakeFailed)`, as it is for a"
    "n empty `chain`; so is one whose\n    key share does not have its group's length (`illegal_parameter`"
    "). The timeouts set on `tcp` apply to\n    every read and write.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}HttpError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export en"
    "um HttpError\u{1f}Why an HTTP request or connection failed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum HttpError\n    in `std::http`\n\n  "
    "  Why an HTTP request or connection failed.\n\n    - `HttpNetFailure(e)`: the network failed, as `e` s"
    "ays.\n    - `HttpTlsFailure(e)`: the TLS connection failed, as `e` says.\n    - `BadUrl`: the URL is m"
    "alformed (`Url::parse`).\n    - `UnsupportedScheme`: the URL's scheme is neither `http` nor `https`.\n"
    "    - `NoRoots`: an https request needed the system's trusted roots and `TrustStore::system` failed."
    "\n    - `BadMessage`: an HTTP message received is malformed; or one to be sent would be: a header who"
    "se name\n      is not a token or whose value holds a control byte other than the tab (a CR or LF woul"
    "d start a\n      header or a body of its own), a method that is not a token, or a status outside 100 "
    "to 599; or a\n      server's response with no request waiting for one (`HttpConnection::respond` call"
    "ed twice).\n    - `TooLarge`: a message's head is over 65536 bytes, or its body over the limit.\n    -"
    " `TooManyRedirects`: a response asked for one redirect more than the client's `max_redirects`.\n    -"
    " `ConnectionClosed`: the connection ended inside a message.\n\n    Variants:\n        HttpNetFailure(Ne"
    "tError)\n        HttpTlsFailure(TlsError)\n        BadUrl\n        UnsupportedScheme\n        NoRoots\n  "
    "      BadMessage\n        TooLarge\n        TooManyRedirects\n        ConnectionClosed\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Http"
    "Error::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpError::text(ref<HttpError, shared> e) : str\u{1f}A one-line description of t"
    "he error, for messages.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpError::text(ref<HttpError, shared> e) : str\n    in `std::http"
    "`\n\n    A one-line description of the error, for messages.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Url\u{1f}A"
    " parsed absolute URL, `scheme://host[:port]/path?query`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Url\n    in `std::http`\n\n    "
    "A parsed absolute URL, `scheme://host[:port]/path?query`.\n\n    - `scheme`: lower-cased.\n    - `host`"
    ": lower-cased; an IPv6 host keeps its brackets (`[::1]`).\n    - `port`: the number after the host's "
    "`:`, or the scheme's default: 443 for `https`, 80 otherwise.\n    - `path`: \"/\" when the text has non"
    "e.\n    - `query`: the text after `?`, without it; empty when there is none.\n\n    The fragment (`#…"
    "`), which never reaches a server, is dropped.\n\n    Fields:\n        String scheme\n        String host"
    "\n        u16 port\n        String path\n        String query\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Url::"
    "parse(StringView text) : Result<Url, HttpError>\u{1f}Parses an absolute URL.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Url::parse(String"
    "View text) : Result<Url, HttpError>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    Parses an absolute URL.\n\n    `Err(BadUrl"
    ")` for text without `://`; with an empty host, whether or not a port follows; with a host\n    that i"
    "s neither a name of RFC 3986's `reg-name` characters (letters, digits, `-._~!$&'()*+,;=` and\n    `%`"
    ") nor a bracketed IPv6 address; with user information (`user@`); with a port that is not 1 to 5\n    "
    "decimal digits up to 65535 (no sign); or with a space, a control byte or DEL anywhere in the text,\n "
    "   which a request line or `Host` header would otherwise carry into the request (a space in a path i"
    "s\n    written `%20`). The scheme is not checked here: `HttpClient::send` gives `Err(UnsupportedSchem"
    "e)` for\n    one that is neither `http` nor `https`.\n\n    Example, \"Url::parse: defaults and normalis"
    "ation\":\n        Url u = Result::unwrap(Url::parse(\"HTTPS://Example.com/a/b?x=1#top\"));\n        asser"
    "t(u.scheme == \"https\" && u.host == \"example.com\" && u.port == 443);\n        assert(u.path == \"/a/b\" "
    "&& u.query == \"x=1\");\n        assert(Url::target(&u) == \"/a/b?x=1\");\n        Url v = Result::unwrap("
    "Url::parse(\"http://[::1]:8080\"));\n        assert(v.host == \"[::1]\" && v.path == \"/\");\n        assert"
    "(Url::text(&v) == \"http://[::1]:8080/\");\n        assert(Result::is_err(&Url::parse(\"http://user@exam"
    "ple.com/\")));\n\n    Example, \"Url::parse: what cannot be written into a request\":\n        assert(Resu"
    "lt::is_err(&Url::parse(\"http://:8080/x\")));\n        assert(Result::is_err(&Url::parse(\"http://host:+"
    "80/\")));\n        assert(Result::is_err(&Url::parse(\"http://example.com/a b\")));\n        assert(Resul"
    "t::is_err(&Url::parse(\"http://example.com/x\\r\\nX-Evil: 1\")));\n        assert(Result::is_err(&Url::pa"
    "rse(\"http://exa mple.com/\")));\n        assert(Result::is_err(&Url::parse(\"http://exa\\\"mple.com/\")));"
    "\n        assert(Result::is_err(&Url::parse(\"http://[::1/\")));\n        assert(Result::unwrap(Url::par"
    "se(\"http://127.0.0.1:65535/a%20b\")).port == 65535);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::target\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Url::target"
    "(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\u{1f}The request target: the path, then `?` and the query when the query is"
    " not empty.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Url::target(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The request "
    "target: the path, then `?` and the query when the query is not empty.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn Url::text(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\u{1f}The URL as text again, with the port only when it is not"
    " the scheme's default.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Url::text(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The"
    " URL as text again, with the port only when it is not the scheme's default.\n\n    The fragment, dropp"
    "ed by `Url::parse`, does not come back.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}percent_encode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn percent_encode(slice"
    "<u8, shared> bytes) : String\u{1f}Percent-encodes `bytes` as RFC 3986 does: unreserved bytes as they are,"
    " every other as `%XX`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn percent_encode(slice<u8, shared> bytes) : String\n    in `std::http"
    "`\n\n    Percent-encodes `bytes` as RFC 3986 does: unreserved bytes as they are, every other as `%XX`."
    "\n\n    The unreserved bytes are ASCII letters and digits, `-`, `.`, `_` and `~`; the hex digits are u"
    "pper\n    case. A space becomes `%20`; `form_encode` writes it as `+`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}percent_decode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn percent_decode(StringView text) : Option<Vec<u8>>\u{1f}The bytes `text` percent-encodes, each `"
    "%XX` decoded.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn percent_decode(StringView text) : Option<Vec<u8>>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    T"
    "he bytes `text` percent-encodes, each `%XX` decoded.\n\n    `None` for a `%` not followed by two hex d"
    "igits; hex digits of either case are read. A `+` stays\n    a `+`; `form_decode` reads it as a space."
    "\n\n    Example, \"percent_decode: the reverse of percent_encode\":\n        assert(percent_encode(String"
    "View::as_bytes(\"a b/ü\")) == \"a%20b%2F%C3%BC\");\n        Vec<u8> back = Option::unwrap(percent_decode"
    "(\"a%20b%2f\"));\n        assert(Result::unwrap(String::from_utf8(back)) == \"a b/\");\n        assert(Opt"
    "ion::is_none(&percent_decode(\"100%\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Param\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Param\u{1f}One name and va"
    "lue of a query string or an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Param\n    in `s"
    "td::http`\n\n    One name and value of a query string or an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body.\n"
    "\n    Names compare exactly (`find_param`), unlike a header's.\n\n    Fields:\n        String name\n     "
    "   String value\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Param::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Param::new(StringView name, StringView value) : "
    "Param\u{1f}A parameter with a copy of `name` and of `value`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Param::new(StringView name, Strin"
    "gView value) : Param\n    in `std::http`\n\n    A parameter with a copy of `name` and of `value`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std"
    "::http\u{1f}find_param\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn find_param(slice<Param, shared> params, StringView name) : Option<Str"
    "ingView> from params\u{1f}The value of the first parameter named exactly `name`, or `None` when there is "
    "none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn find_param(slice<Param, shared> params, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from "
    "params\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The value of the first parameter named exactly `name`, or `None` when"
    " there is none.\n\n    The comparison is case-sensitive, unlike `find_header`'s.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}form_deco"
    "de\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn form_decode(StringView text) : Vec<Param>\u{1f}The parameters of a query string (without "
    "its `?`) or of an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn form_decode(StringView text) "
    ": Vec<Param>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The parameters of a query string (without its `?`) or of an `ap"
    "plication/x-www-form-urlencoded` body.\n\n    The text is split into `name=value` pairs at `&` only, a"
    "nd empty pairs are skipped; a `;` is part of a\n    name or value, as the WHATWG URL standard reads i"
    "t (splitting at `;` too would let a cache or proxy\n    that splits at `&` see other parameters than "
    "the program does). A pair without `=` has an empty value.\n    Each name and value is read with `+` a"
    "s a space and then percent-decoded; one that is not UTF-8 after\n    decoding, or holds a bad escape,"
    " is kept as given, so nothing is lost.\n\n    Example, \"form_decode: pairs, bare names and bad escapes"
    "\":\n        Vec<Param> ps = form_decode(\"q=red+fish&flag&&n=%41&x=%zz;role=admin\");\n        assert(Ve"
    "c::len(&ps) == 4);\n        assert(Option::unwrap(find_param(&ps, \"q\")) == \"red fish\");\n        asser"
    "t(Option::unwrap(find_param(&ps, \"flag\")) == \"\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(find_param(&ps, \"n\")"
    ") == \"A\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(find_param(&ps, \"x\")) == \"%zz;role=admin\");\n        assert("
    "Option::is_none(&find_param(&ps, \"role\")));\n        assert(Option::is_none(&find_param(&ps, \"Q\")));\n"
    "\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}form_encode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn form_encode(slice<Param, shared> params) : String\u{1f}Encodes `para"
    "ms` as a query string or form body that `form_decode` reads back.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn form_encode(slice<Param"
    ", shared> params) : String\n    in `std::http`\n\n    Encodes `params` as a query string or form body t"
    "hat `form_decode` reads back.\n\n    The pairs are `name=value`, joined by `&`, each name and value pe"
    "rcent-encoded with a space as `+`.\n    There is no leading `?`.\n\n    Example, \"form_encode: spaces a"
    "nd reserved bytes\":\n        Vec<Param> ps = Vec::new();\n        Vec::push(&mut ps, Param::new(\"q\", \""
    "a b&c\"));\n        Vec::push(&mut ps, Param::new(\"lang\", \"en\"));\n        String body = form_encode(&p"
    "s);\n        assert(body == \"q=a+b%26c&lang=en\");\n        Vec<Param> back = form_decode(&body);\n     "
    "   assert(back[0].value == \"a b&c\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::query_pairs\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Url::query_pairs(ref<"
    "Url, shared> u) : Vec<Param>\u{1f}The parameters of the URL's query, as `form_decode` reads them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export"
    " fn Url::query_pairs(ref<Url, shared> u) : Vec<Param>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The parameters of the "
    "URL's query, as `form_decode` reads them.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Header\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Header\u{1f}One header "
    "field: a name and a value.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Header\n    in `std::http`\n\n    One header field: a name an"
    "d a value.\n\n    Names compare without regard to ASCII case (`find_header`).\n\n    Fields:\n        Str"
    "ing name\n        String value\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Header::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Header::new(StringView name, Stri"
    "ngView value) : Header\u{1f}A header with a copy of `name` and of `value`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Header::new(StringV"
    "iew name, StringView value) : Header\n    in `std::http`\n\n    A header with a copy of `name` and of `"
    "value`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}find_header\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn find_header(slice<Header, shared> headers, StringView n"
    "ame) : Option<StringView> from headers\u{1f}The value of the first header named `name`, ignoring ASCII ca"
    "se, or `None` when there is none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn find_header(slice<Header, shared> headers, StringView n"
    "ame) : Option<StringView> from headers\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The value of the first header named `"
    "name`, ignoring ASCII case, or `None` when there is none.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Request\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct R"
    "equest\u{1f}An HTTP request: the method, the URL, the headers and the body.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Request\n    in"
    " `std::http`\n\n    An HTTP request: the method, the URL, the headers and the body.\n\n    For the clien"
    "t, `url` is absolute (`https://…`); for a request a server received, it is the target as\n    sent "
    "(`/path?query`). A server's request has the body decoded if it came chunked.\n\n    Fields:\n        St"
    "ring method\n        String url\n        Vec<Header> headers\n        Vec<u8> body\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Request:"
    ":new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Request::new(StringView method, StringView url) : Request\u{1f}A request with `method` "
    "and `url`, no headers and an empty body.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Request::new(StringView method, StringView url) "
    ": Request\n    in `std::http`\n\n    A request with `method` and `url`, no headers and an empty body.\n\u{1f}"
    "\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Request::header\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Request::header(ref<Request, shared> r, StringView name) : O"
    "ption<StringView> from r\u{1f}The value of the request's first header named `name`, ignoring ASCII case.\u{1f}"
    "\u{1f}export fn Request::header(ref<Request, shared> r, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from r\n    "
    "in `std::http`\n\n    The value of the request's first header named `name`, ignoring ASCII case.\n\n    "
    "Example, \"Request::header: names ignore case\":\n        Request r = Request::new(\"POST\", \"https://exa"
    "mple.com/upload\");\n        Vec::push(&mut r.headers, Header::new(\"Content-Type\", \"text/plain\"));\n   "
    "     assert(Option::unwrap(Request::header(&r, \"content-type\")) == \"text/plain\");\n        assert(Opt"
    "ion::is_none(&Request::header(&r, \"accept\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Response\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Response\u{1f}An"
    " HTTP response: the status, its reason phrase, the headers and the whole body.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Respon"
    "se\n    in `std::http`\n\n    An HTTP response: the status, its reason phrase, the headers and the whol"
    "e body.\n\n    The client gives the body decoded if it came chunked, and decompressed if it came with\n"
    "    `Content-Encoding: gzip` or `deflate` (that header and `Content-Length` are then dropped).\n\n    "
    "Fields:\n        u16 status\n        String reason\n        Vec<Header> headers\n        Vec<u8> body\n\u{1f}\u{1e}"
    "std::http\u{1f}Response::header\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Response::header(ref<Response, shared> r, StringView name) :"
    " Option<StringView> from r\u{1f}The value of the response's first header named `name`, ignoring ASCII cas"
    "e.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Response::header(ref<Response, shared> r, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from r"
    "\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The value of the response's first header named `name`, ignoring ASCII case."
    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Response::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Response::text(ref<Response, shared> r) : Result<String, Ut"
    "f8Error>\u{1f}The body as text: a copy of its bytes, which must be UTF-8.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Response::text(ref<R"
    "esponse, shared> r) : Result<String, Utf8Error>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The body as text: a copy of "
    "its bytes, which must be UTF-8.\n\n    `Err(e)` when they are not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}reason_phrase\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export"
    " fn reason_phrase(u16 status) : str\u{1f}The reason phrase RFC 9110 gives a status code, such as \"Not Fou"
    "nd\" for 404.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn reason_phrase(u16 status) : str\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The reason phrase RF"
    "C 9110 gives a status code, such as \"Not Found\" for 404.\n\n    \"\" for a status it does not list here."
    "\n\n    Example, \"reason_phrase: unlisted codes\":\n        assert(reason_phrase(404) == \"Not Found\");\n "
    "       assert(reason_phrase(422) == \"Unprocessable Content\");\n        assert(reason_phrase(410) == \""
    "Gone\");\n        assert(reason_phrase(299) == \"\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}HttpClient\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struc"
    "t HttpClient\u{1f}An HTTP/1.1 client: the settings and the state it carries from request to request.\u{1f}\u{1f}exp"
    "ort struct HttpClient\n    in `std::http::client`\n\n    An HTTP/1.1 client: the settings and the state"
    " it carries from request to request.\n\n    - `roots`: the trusted roots https verifies servers agains"
    "t; `None` until the first https request\n      loads the system's (`TrustStore::system`), or a store "
    "the program puts there.\n    - `timeout_ms`: the timeout for connecting and for each read and write, "
    "in milliseconds.\n    - `max_redirects`: how many redirects `send` follows; 0 follows none, and `send"
    "` gives the 3xx response\n      itself (its `Location` and `Set-Cookie` there to read).\n    - `max_bo"
    "dy`: the most bytes a response body may have, after decompression too (`TooLarge` beyond).\n    - `he"
    "aders`: sent with every request; a request's own header of the same name replaces one.\n    - `keep_a"
    "live`: when set, the last connection is kept open while the server allows, and the next\n      reques"
    "t to the same origin goes on it; when not (the default), each request has its own connection.\n\n    A"
    " program that makes several https requests keeps one client, so the roots are loaded once.\n\n    Fiel"
    "ds:\n        Option<TrustStore> roots\n        u64 timeout_ms\n        usize max_redirects\n        usiz"
    "e max_body\n        Vec<Header> headers\n        bool keep_alive\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}HttpClient::new\u{1f}f"
    "n\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::new() : HttpClient\u{1f}A client with the default settings.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpClient"
    "::new() : HttpClient\n    in `std::http::client`\n\n    A client with the default settings.\n\n    No roo"
    "ts loaded yet, a 30 s timeout, up to 10 redirects, a 16 MiB body limit, `keep_alive` off, and\n    th"
    "e headers `User-Agent` and `Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate`.\n\n    Example, \"HttpClient::new: the def"
    "aults\":\n        HttpClient c = HttpClient::new();\n        assert(c.timeout_ms == 30000 && c.max_redi"
    "rects == 10 && !c.keep_alive);\n        assert(Option::is_none(&c.roots));\n        assert(Option::is_"
    "some(&find_header(&c.headers, \"user-agent\")));\n        c.max_body = 1_048_576;\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}H"
    "ttpClient::send\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::send(ref<HttpClient, exclusive> c, ref<Request, shared> req"
    ") : Result<Response, HttpError>\u{1f}Sends `req` and gives the final response, following redirects.\u{1f}\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn HttpClient::send(ref<HttpClient, exclusive> c, ref<Request, shared> req) : Result<Response, Ht"
    "tpError>\n    in `std::http::client`\n\n    Sends `req` and gives the final response, following redirec"
    "ts.\n\n    - `req.url` is absolute; a scheme other than `http` or `https` is `Err(UnsupportedScheme)`."
    " The\n      host's addresses are tried in turn.\n    - The request carries `Host`, the client's header"
    "s and then the request's own (`Host`,\n      `Content-Length`, `Connection` and `Transfer-Encoding`, "
    "the client's or the request's, are ignored:\n      `send` frames the body itself), `Content-Length` w"
    "hen the body is not\n      empty or the method is POST, PUT or PATCH, and `Connection: close` unless "
    "`keep_alive` is set.\n    - A method that is not a token, or a header (the client's or the request's)"
    " whose name is not a token\n      or whose value holds a control byte other than the tab, is `Err(Bad"
    "Message)` before anything is\n      sent: a CR LF taken from data would otherwise end the line and in"
    "ject headers or a second request.\n    - Interim responses (status 1xx) are read past, up to 16 of th"
    "em; one more is `Err(BadMessage)`. A\n      body sent with `Content-Encoding: gzip` or `deflate` arri"
    "ves decoded.\n    - A 301, 302 or 303 with a `Location` is followed by GET without the body (HEAD sta"
    "ys HEAD), a 307 or\n      308 with the method and body kept; a redirect without `Location` is given a"
    "s it is. `Location` is a\n      URI reference resolved against the request's URL as RFC 3986 §5 reso"
    "lves one (an absolute URL, `//`\n      and a host, an absolute path, `?` and a query, or a path relat"
    "ive to the current one, with `.` and\n      `..` segments removed); its fragment is dropped. With `ma"
    "x_redirects` 0 no redirect is followed and\n      the 3xx response is given; otherwise one redirect m"
    "ore than `max_redirects` is\n      `Err(TooManyRedirects)`. Once a redirect leaves the request's orig"
    "in\n      (scheme, host and port), `Authorization`, `Proxy-Authorization` and `Cookie`, the client's "
    "and the\n      request's, are not sent again.\n    - On a kept connection that proves closed before an"
    "y of the response arrives, an idempotent request\n      (GET, HEAD, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS, TRACE) is s"
    "ent again on a fresh connection; another is\n      `Err(ConnectionClosed)`, since the server may have"
    " acted on it.\n    - Network and TLS failures are `Err(HttpNetFailure(e))` and `Err(HttpTlsFailure(e)"
    ")`; see `HttpError`\n      for the rest.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}http_get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn http_get(StringVie"
    "w url) : Result<Response, HttpError>\u{1f}Sends a GET of `url` with a fresh `HttpClient::new()` and gives"
    " the response.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn http_get(StringView url) : Result<Response, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::"
    "client`\n\n    Sends a GET of `url` with a fresh `HttpClient::new()` and gives the response.\n\n    For "
    "https each call loads the system's roots again; a program that makes several requests keeps an\n    `"
    "HttpClient`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}http_post\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn http_post(StringView url, StringView content"
    "_type, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<Response, HttpError>\u{1f}Sends a POST of `body` to `url`, with `"
    "Content-Type: content_type`, from a fresh default client.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn http_post(StringView url, Strin"
    "gView content_type, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<Response, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::client`"
    "\n\n    Sends a POST of `body` to `url`, with `Content-Type: content_type`, from a fresh default clien"
    "t.\n\n    As `http_get`, a program that makes several requests keeps an `HttpClient`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::ser"
    "ver\u{1f}HttpServer\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct HttpServer\u{1f}A listening HTTP/1.1 server: `accept` gives "
    "each client's connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct HttpServer\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    A liste"
    "ning HTTP/1.1 server: `accept` gives each client's connection.\n\n    - `max_body`: the most bytes a r"
    "equest body may have (`TooLarge` beyond); 16 MiB from `bind`.\n    - `timeout_ms`: the timeout for ea"
    "ch read and write on the connections it accepts, in milliseconds;\n      30 s from `bind`. A request'"
    "s head (its request line and headers) must also arrive whole within it,\n      from its first byte: a"
    " client that sends it a byte at a time cannot hold a connection longer.\n\n    The limits apply to eve"
    "ry connection accepted after they are set. A server program handles each\n    connection in a thread "
    "of its own (`spawn`). Dropping the server closes its listening socket.\n\n    Fields:\n        usize ma"
    "x_body\n        u64 timeout_ms\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::bind\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind(Soc"
    "ketAddr a) : Result<HttpServer, NetError>\u{1f}An HTTP server listening at `a`, with a 16 MiB body limit "
    "and a 30 s timeout per read and write.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind(SocketAddr a) : Result<HttpServer"
    ", NetError>\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    An HTTP server listening at `a`, with a 16 MiB body limi"
    "t and a 30 s timeout per read and write.\n\n    Port 0 asks the system for a free port (`local_addr` n"
    "ames it). Errors as `TcpListener::bind`'s.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::bind_tls\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Htt"
    "pServer::bind_tls(SocketAddr a, PrivateKey key, Vec<Certificate> chain) : Result<HttpServer, NetErro"
    "r>\u{1f}An HTTPS server listening at `a`: each connection it accepts first completes a TLS 1.3 handshake."
    "\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind_tls(SocketAddr a, PrivateKey key, Vec<Certificate> chain) : Result<Http"
    "Server, NetError>\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    An HTTPS server listening at `a`: each connection "
    "it accepts first completes a TLS 1.3 handshake.\n\n    `key` is the server's private key and `chain` i"
    "ts certificate first, then its issuers, as\n    `TlsStream::server` takes them; each connection gets "
    "its own copy. The handshake is done by the\n    connection's first `request` or `respond`, on the thr"
    "ead that handles it, not by `accept`. Otherwise\n    as `bind`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::local"
    "_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::local_addr(ref<HttpServer, shared> s) : SocketAddr\u{1f}The address the se"
    "rver listens at, with the port the system chose for port 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::local_addr(ref<Ht"
    "tpServer, shared> s) : SocketAddr\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    The address the server listens at,"
    " with the port the system chose for port 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::accept\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Http"
    "Server::accept(ref<HttpServer, exclusive> s) : Result<HttpConnection, HttpError>\u{1f}Waits for the next "
    "client and gives its connection, with the server's limits and timeouts.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::accep"
    "t(ref<HttpServer, exclusive> s) : Result<HttpConnection, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    "
    "Waits for the next client and gives its connection, with the server's limits and timeouts.\n\n    A fa"
    "ilure of the listener is `Err(HttpNetFailure(e))`. For an https server the TLS handshake is not\n    "
    "done here: the connection's first `request` (or `respond`) does it, on the thread that handles the\n "
    "   connection, so a client that connects and never completes the handshake holds up only its own\n   "
    " connection, not `accept` and the clients after it. A client that fails the handshake is then\n    `E"
    "rr(HttpTlsFailure(e))` from that call, and the connection is closed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnect"
    "ion\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct HttpConnection\u{1f}One client's connection to an `HttpServer`: `reques"
    "t`, then `respond`, repeated while it stays open.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct HttpConnection\n    in `std"
    "::http::server`\n\n    One client's connection to an `HttpServer`: `request`, then `respond`, repeated"
    " while it stays open.\n\n    The connection stays open for the next request when the request is HTTP/1"
    ".1 without `close` among its\n    `Connection` options, or HTTP/1.0 with `keep-alive` among them and "
    "without `close`. Dropping it closes\n    the socket; `close` ends it cleanly first.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::serv"
    "er\u{1f}HttpConnection::peer_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::peer_addr(ref<HttpConnection, shared> c) :"
    " SocketAddr\u{1f}The client's address.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::peer_addr(ref<HttpConnection, shared> c"
    ") : SocketAddr\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    The client's address.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnect"
    "ion::request\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::request(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c) : Result<Option<"
    "Request>, HttpError>\u{1f}Reads the client's next request, or gives `None` when there is none to read.\u{1f}\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn HttpConnection::request(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c) : Result<Option<Request>, HttpErr"
    "or>\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    Reads the client's next request, or gives `None` when there is n"
    "one to read.\n\n    - `Ok(Some(r))`: `r.url` is the target as sent (`/path?query`); the body is read b"
    "y `Content-Length` or\n      chunked encoding, and there is none without them. When an HTTP/1.1 reque"
    "st expects `100-continue`,\n      the `HTTP/1.1 100 Continue` is sent before the body is read, unless"
    " its `Content-Length` is over\n      `max_body` (then `Err(TooLarge)` at once, before the client send"
    "s the body); an HTTP/1.0 request's\n      expectation is ignored.\n    - `Ok(None)`: the client closed"
    " before a request, the server's read timeout (`timeout_ms`) passed before\n      any byte of a next r"
    "equest came (an idle keep-alive connection; the connection then closes), or the\n      last response "
    "ended the connection.\n    - `Err(BadMessage)`: a malformed request line (a method that is not a toke"
    "n, a control byte in the\n      target), header or body, an HTTP/1.1 request without `Host`, a reques"
    "t with two `Host` fields or one\n      whose value is not a host and an optional port, `Content-Lengt"
    "h` fields that disagree, an HTTP/1.0\n      request with `Transfer-Encoding`, or chunked framing that"
    " is not exact (a line not ended by CR LF, a\n      size that is not hex digits from the line's first "
    "byte, a control byte in a chunk extension, a\n      trailer line that is not a header field); `Err(To"
    "oLarge)`: a head, or the trailers, over 65536 bytes,\n      or a body over `max_body`. The caller ans"
    "wers 400 or 413 if it wishes, and the connection then\n      closes. `Err(HttpNetFailure(e))`: the co"
    "nnection failed, or the timeout passed in the middle of a\n      request (`TimedOut`); there is no re"
    "quest to answer, and the connection closes.\n    - On an https connection the first call does the TLS"
    " handshake; a client that fails it is\n      `Err(HttpTlsFailure(e))`, and the connection is closed.\n"
    "\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnection::respond\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::respond(ref<HttpConnection,"
    " exclusive> c, u16 status, slice<Header, shared> headers, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<void, Htt"
    "pError>\u{1f}Writes a response with `status`, `headers` and `body`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::respond(re"
    "f<HttpConnection, exclusive> c, u16 status, slice<Header, shared> headers, slice<u8, shared> body) :"
    " Result<void, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    Writes a response with `status`, `headers` "
    "and `body`.\n\n    The status line carries `reason_phrase(status)`. `Content-Length`, `Transfer-Encodi"
    "ng` and `Connection`\n    among `headers` are dropped, since `respond` frames the body itself: `Conte"
    "nt-Length` is written from\n    `body` (not for 1xx, 204 or 304), `Connection` as negotiated, and `Da"
    "te` (the time now) unless `headers` has one. The body is left out after a HEAD\n    request and for a"
    " status that has none. After a response that ends the connection, the connection is\n    closed and `"
    "request` gives `None`.\n\n    `Err(BadMessage)`, with nothing written, for a status outside 100 to 599"
    ", or a header whose name is not\n    a token or whose value holds a control byte other than the tab: "
    "a CR or LF in a value taken from the\n    request (a redirect's `Location`, a file name) would otherw"
    "ise end the header and let the client write\n    headers and a body of its own (response splitting). "
    "`Err(BadMessage)` too, with nothing written, when\n    no request is waiting for a response: `respond"
    "` answers what the last `request` read (a request, or\n    one it found malformed), once.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http"
    "::server\u{1f}HttpConnection::close\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::close(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c)\u{1f}"
    "Ends the connection: closes its sending side, or sends TLS's close_notify on an https connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn HttpConnection::close(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c)\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    End"
    "s the connection: closes its sending side, or sends TLS's close_notify on an https connection.\n\n    "
    "Does nothing on a connection already closed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}scram_salted_password\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn scra"
    "m_salted_password(StringView password, slice<u8, shared> salt, usize iterations) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}The SCRAM"
    "-SHA-256 salted password: PBKDF2 over HMAC-SHA-256 of `password` and `salt`, 32 bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn sc"
    "ram_salted_password(StringView password, slice<u8, shared> salt, usize iterations) : Vec<u8>\n    in "
    "`std::database`\n\n    The SCRAM-SHA-256 salted password: PBKDF2 over HMAC-SHA-256 of `password` and `"
    "salt`, 32 bytes.\n\n    `iterations` is the server's count. The password is used as given: RFC 5802 pr"
    "epares it with SASLprep\n    first (`saslprep`), as the PostgreSQL client does before `Scram::respond"
    "`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Scram\u{1f}The client's side of one SCRAM-SHA-256 exchange "
    "(RFC 5802, RFC 7677), without channel binding.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Scram\n    in `std::database`\n\n    The "
    "client's side of one SCRAM-SHA-256 exchange (RFC 5802, RFC 7677), without channel binding.\n\n    The "
    "steps in order: `Scram::start`, send `Scram::client_first`, answer the server's first message with\n "
    "   `Scram::respond`, then check the server's final message with `Scram::verify`. The PostgreSQL clie"
    "nt uses\n    it; it is exported so a program can speak the exchange to another server.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::databas"
    "e\u{1f}Scram::start\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Scram::start(StringView user, StringView client_nonce) : Scram\u{1f}A new exc"
    "hange for `user` with the client's nonce `client_nonce`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::start(StringView user, St"
    "ringView client_nonce) : Scram\n    in `std::database`\n\n    A new exchange for `user` with the client"
    "'s nonce `client_nonce`.\n\n    `,` and `=` in `user` are escaped as `=2C` and `=3D`. The nonce should"
    " be fresh random text for each\n    exchange, such as the base64 of bytes from `os_random_bytes`. Pos"
    "tgreSQL ignores the user, and its client\n    sends `\"\"`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::client_first\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn Scram::client_first(ref<Scram, shared> s) : String\u{1f}The client's first message, `n,,n=USER,r=NO"
    "NCE`: no channel binding.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::client_first(ref<Scram, shared> s) : String\n    in `std:"
    ":database`\n\n    The client's first message, `n,,n=USER,r=NONCE`: no channel binding.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database"
    "\u{1f}Scram::respond\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Scram::respond(ref<Scram, exclusive> s, StringView server_first, String"
    "View password) : Result<String, PgError>\u{1f}The client's final message, carrying the proof of `password"
    "`, for the server's first message.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::respond(ref<Scram, exclusive> s, StringView ser"
    "ver_first, StringView password) : Result<String, PgError>\n    in `std::database`\n\n    The client's f"
    "inal message, carrying the proof of `password`, for the server's first message.\n\n    `server_first` "
    "is the server's `r=…,s=…,i=…`. Remembers the signature `Scram::verify` then expects.\n    `Err("
    "AuthFailed)` when the server's nonce does not begin with the client's and add to it;\n    `Err(Protoc"
    "olViolation)` when the message is malformed, asks for an extension (`m=`), gives an iteration\n    co"
    "unt of 0 or a salt that is not base64.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::verify\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Scram::verify(ref<"
    "Scram, shared> s, StringView server_final) : bool\u{1f}Whether the server's final message (`v=…`) carri"
    "es the signature this exchange expects.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::verify(ref<Scram, shared> s, StringView se"
    "rver_final) : bool\n    in `std::database`\n\n    Whether the server's final message (`v=…`) carries "
    "the signature this exchange expects.\n\n    `false` for anything else, an `e=` error among them, and `"
    "false` before `Scram::respond` has succeeded\n    (there is no signature to expect yet).\n\n    Example"
    ", \"Scram: a whole exchange\":\n        Scram s = Scram::start(\"user\", \"rOprNGfwEbeRWgbNEkqO\");\n       "
    " assert(Scram::client_first(&s) == \"n,,n=user,r=rOprNGfwEbeRWgbNEkqO\");\n        String first = \"r=rO"
    "prNGfwEbeRWgbNEkqO%hvYDpWUa2RaTCAfuxFIlj)hNlF$k0,\";\n        String::append(&mut first, \"s=W22ZaJ0SNY"
    "7soEsUEjb6gQ==,i=4\");\n        String reply = Result::unwrap(Scram::respond(&mut s, &first, \"pencil\")"
    ");\n        assert(StringView::ends_with(&reply, \",p=0ByS2g6XZEtov8MR140MFRsEfy8/X+bacfpPofVtKjE=\"));"
    "\n        assert(Scram::verify(&s, \"v=ITrN4zX09+hsD398Qk6ol73eg0shWPnOWwnwS83jitc=\"));\n        assert"
    "(!Scram::verify(&s, \"e=invalid-proof\"));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}saslprep\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn saslprep(StringView t"
    "ext) : Option<String>\u{1f}`text` prepared by SASLprep (RFC 4013), as PostgreSQL prepares the passwords i"
    "t stores and libpq the password it sends; `None` when the result is prohibited.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn saslprep("
    "StringView text) : Option<String>\n    in `std::database`\n\n    `text` prepared by SASLprep (RFC 4013)"
    ", as PostgreSQL prepares the passwords it stores and libpq the\n    password it sends; `None` when th"
    "e result is prohibited.\n\n    The steps of stringprep (RFC 3454) with the SASLprep profile, over Unic"
    "ode 3.2, in the order and on the\n    text PostgreSQL's own SASLprep uses: ASCII text comes back unch"
    "anged, controls included; otherwise the\n    non-ASCII spaces of table C.1.2 (no-break space, U+200B "
    "zero width space and the others) become U+0020\n    and the characters of table B.1 (soft hyphen, zer"
    "o-width joiners, variation selectors) are removed;\n    `None` when nothing is left; then `None` when"
    " the mapped text holds a character of the prohibited\n    tables (C.1.2, C.2.1, C.2.2, C.3 to C.9: co"
    "ntrols, private use, non-characters, surrogates, tagging and\n    the bidirectional controls) or a co"
    "de point Unicode 3.2 leaves unassigned (table A.1, the rule for stored\n    strings), or breaks the b"
    "idirectional rule (text with a right-to-left character holds no left-to-right\n    one and begins and"
    " ends with a right-to-left one); these checks read the mapped text before\n    normalisation, as Post"
    "greSQL's do. The result is the mapped text normalised to NFKC (with Corrigendum #4,\n    as every Uni"
    "code version after 3.2). A client that gets `None` uses the password as given, as libpq does.\n\n    E"
    "xample, \"saslprep: the RFC's examples\":\n        assert(Option::unwrap(saslprep(\"I\\u{AD}X\")) == \"IX\")"
    ";\n        assert(Option::unwrap(saslprep(\"user\")) == \"user\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(saslprep"
    "(\"USER\")) == \"USER\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(saslprep(\"\\u{AA}\")) == \"a\");\n        assert(Opti"
    "on::unwrap(saslprep(\"\\u{2168}\")) == \"IX\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(saslprep(\"\\u{7}\")) == \"\\u{7"
    "}\");\n        assert(Option::is_none(&saslprep(\"\\u{627}1\")));\n        assert(Option::unwrap(saslprep("
    "\"a\\u{A0}b\")) == \"a b\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(saslprep(\"\\u{D55C}\")) == \"\\u{D55C}\");\n        "
    "assert(Option::unwrap(saslprep(\"e\\u{301}\")) == \"\\u{E9}\");\n        assert(Option::is_none(&saslprep(\""
    "\\u{221}\\u{A0}x\")));\n\n    Example, \"saslprep: as PostgreSQL's\":\n        assert(Option::unwrap(saslpre"
    "p(\"x\\u{200B}z\")) == \"x z\");\n        assert(Option::is_none(&saslprep(\"\\u{AD}\\u{200D}\")));\n        as"
