    "time parameter `name` at startup; `None` when it gave none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::parameter(ref<P"
    "gConnection, shared> c, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from c\n    in `std::database::postgres"
    "`\n\n    The value the server reported for the run-time parameter `name` at startup; `None` when it ga"
    "ve none.\n\n    Such as `server_version`, `server_encoding` or `TimeZone`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}P"
    "gConnection::set_timeout_ms\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::set_timeout_ms(ref<PgConnection, exclusive> c"
    ", u64 ms)\u{1f}Sets the timeout, in milliseconds, for each read and write on the connection from now on, "
    "the wait for a statement's reply included; 0 waits for ever.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::set_timeout_ms"
    "(ref<PgConnection, exclusive> c, u64 ms)\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    Sets the timeout, in "
    "milliseconds, for each read and write on the connection from now on, the wait for a\n    statement's "
    "reply included; 0 waits for ever.\n\n    A statement that may run longer than the timeout `connect` or"
    " `connect_with` set (a report, a migration,\n    `CREATE INDEX`) is run after a larger one, or 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}s"
    "td::database::postgres\u{1f}PgConnection::query\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::query(ref<PgConnection, exclus"
    "ive> c, StringView sql, slice<PgValue, shared> params) : Result<PgResult, PgError>\u{1f}Runs one statemen"
    "t with `$1`, `$2`, ...\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::query(ref<PgConnection, exclusive> c, StringView sql"
    ", slice<PgValue, shared> params) : Result<PgResult, PgError>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    R"
    "uns one statement with `$1`, `$2`, ... bound to `params`, and gives its result.\n\n    A server error "
    "is `Err(Server(e))` once the server is ready again, and the connection stays usable\n    (unless the "
    "server ended the session: a `FATAL` error is given as `Server(e)` too, and the connection is\n    the"
    "n closed); `Err(ResultTooLarge)` when the rows exceed `max_result`, also leaving it usable. A\n    `C"
    "OPY` is `Err(Unsupported(_))`, the connection usable. A network or protocol failure closes the\n    c"
    "onnection, and every later call gives `Err(Disconnected)`. Transactions are statements: `BEGIN`,\n   "
    " `COMMIT`, `ROLLBACK`.\n\n    When the reply does not come within the connection's timeout, the statem"
    "ent is cancelled (a\n    CancelRequest, as libpq's `PQcancel` sends) and the reply waited for once mo"
    "re: what is given is then\n    what the server did, a cancelled statement's `Err(Server(e))` (SQLSTAT"
    "E `57014`) or the result of a\n    statement that completed first, and the connection stays usable. O"
    "nly when that wait times out as well\n    is the connection closed with `Err(PgNetFailure(TimedOut))`"
    ", and the statement may then have completed\n    or not. `PgConnection::set_timeout_ms` sets a longer"
    " timeout, or none.\n    A statement without parameters takes an empty slice: `array<PgValue, 0> none "
    "= [];` and `&none` (a bare\n    `&[]` is an `array<i32, 0>`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgConnection:"
