    "j` back.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::json\u{1f}Json::pretty\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Json::pretty(ref<Json, shared> j) : String\u{1f}"
    "The value `j` as JSON text for people: one element or member per line, two spaces per level.\u{1f}\u{1f}export"
    " fn Json::pretty(ref<Json, shared> j) : String\n    in `std::encoding::json`\n\n    The value `j` as JS"
    "ON text for people: one element or member per line, two spaces per level.\n\n    A key is followed by "
    "`: `, an empty array or object stays `[]` or `{}`, and there is no newline at the\n    end. Numbers a"
    "nd strings are written as `Json::text` writes them.\n\n    Example, \"Json::pretty: the layout\":\n      "
    "  Json a = JsonArray(Vec::new());\n        Json::push(&mut a, JsonNull);\n        Json::push(&mut a, J"
    "sonText(\"x\"));\n        String p = Json::pretty(&a);\n        assert(p == \"[\\n  null,\\n  \\\"x\\\"\\n]\");\n\u{1f}"
    "\u{1e}std::encoding::json\u{1f}Json::get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Json::get(ref<Json, shared> j, StringView key) : Option<"
