    "The bytes as lowercase hexadecimal text, two digits each.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn to_hex(slice<u8, shared> bytes)"
    " : String\n    in `std::encoding::hex`\n\n    The bytes as lowercase hexadecimal text, two digits each."
    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::hex\u{1f}from_hex\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn from_hex(StringView text) : Result<Vec<u8>, ParseError>\u{1f}"
    "The bytes the hexadecimal `text` spells, two digits a byte, in either case.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn from_hex(Stri"
    "ngView text) : Result<Vec<u8>, ParseError>\n    in `std::encoding::hex`\n\n    The bytes the hexadecima"
    "l `text` spells, two digits a byte, in either case.\n\n    The empty text is no bytes, so `from_hex(to"
    "_hex(b))` gives `b` back for every `b`, the empty one too (as\n    `base64_decode` does).\n\n    - `Err"
    "(Invalid(i))` at the first byte that is not a hexadecimal digit.\n    - `Err(Invalid(len))` when the "
    "digits are odd in number.\n\n    Example, \"from_hex: either case in, lowercase out\":\n        Vec<u8> b"
    " = Result::unwrap(from_hex(\"00FFa0\"));\n        assert(Vec::len(&b) == 3);\n        assert(b[1] == 255"
    ");\n        String h = to_hex(&b);\n        assert(h == \"00ffa0\");\n        match (from_hex(\"abc\"))\n   "
    "     {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i == 3),\n            _               : assert(false),\n  "
    "      }\n        // Report 287: no bytes round-trip.\n        assert(Vec::len(&Result::unwrap(from_hex"
    "(\"\"))) == 0);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::base64\u{1f}base64_encode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn base64_encode(slice<u8, shared> byt"
    "es) : String\u{1f}The bytes in base64 (RFC 4648 §4), padded with `=` to a multiple of four characters.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "export fn base64_encode(slice<u8, shared> bytes) : String\n    in `std::encoding::base64`\n\n    The by"
    "tes in base64 (RFC 4648 §4), padded with `=` to a multiple of four characters.\n\n    The alphabet is"
    " the standard one: `A`-`Z`, `a`-`z`, `0`-`9`, `+` and `/`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::base64\u{1f}base64_decode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn base64_decode(StringView text) : Result<Vec<u8>, ParseError>\u{1f}The bytes the base64 `text` s"
    "pells, read as `base64_encode` writes it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn base64_decode(StringView text) : Result<Vec<u8>"
    ", ParseError>\n    in `std::encoding::base64`\n\n    The bytes the base64 `text` spells, read as `base6"
    "4_encode` writes it.\n\n    Padding is required. Empty text gives no bytes.\n\n    - `Err(Invalid(len))`"
    " when the length is not a multiple of four.\n    - `Err(Invalid(i))` at the first byte that is not a "
    "base64 character; a `=` before the final one or two is\n      such a byte.\n    - `Err(Invalid(i))` at"
    " the last character before the padding when it leaves bits over that are not\n      zero: `\"QR==\"` is"
    " refused, since `base64_encode` writes `\"A\"` as `\"QQ==\"`. Each byte string has one\n      text.\n\n    "
    "Example, \"base64_decode: padding\":\n        StringView text = \"hi!?\";\n        String e = base64_encod"
    "e(StringView::as_bytes(text));\n        assert(e == \"aGkhPw==\");\n        Vec<u8> d = Result::unwrap(b"
    "ase64_decode(&e));\n        assert(Vec::len(&d) == 4);\n        match (base64_decode(\"aG=hPw==\"))\n    "
    "    {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i == 2),\n            _               : assert(false),\n   "
    "     }\n        match (base64_decode(\"QR==\"))\n        {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i == 1),"
    "\n            _               : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum "
    "Toml\u{1f}A TOML value: a string, an integer, a float, a boolean, a date-time, an array or a table.\u{1f}\u{1f}expo"
    "rt enum Toml\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    A TOML value: a string, an integer, a float, a boolea"
    "n, a date-time, an array or a table.\n\n    - `TomlString(s)`: a string, its escapes decoded.\n    - `T"
    "omlInteger(i)`: an integer, exact in `i64`.\n    - `TomlFloat(x)`: a float, `inf` and `nan` included."
    "\n    - `TomlBool(b)`: `true` or `false`.\n    - `TomlDateTime(d)`: one of the four date-time forms (s"
    "ee `TomlDateTime`).\n    - `TomlArray(items)`: the elements, in order; elements may be of different k"
    "inds.\n    - `TomlTable(members)`: the members in the order read or added; a key occurs once.\n\n    Th"
    "e variant names carry `Toml` so that none clashes with another `std` enum's. Dropping a `Toml` frees"
    " the\n    whole tree.\n\n    Variants:\n        TomlString(String)\n        TomlInteger(i64)\n        Toml"
    "Float(f64)\n        TomlBool(bool)\n        TomlDateTime(TomlDateTime)\n        TomlArray(Vec<Toml>)\n  "
    "      TomlTable(Vec<TomlMember>)\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}TomlMember\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct TomlMember\u{1f}On"
    "e member of a TOML table: its key and its value.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct TomlMember\n    in `std::encoding::to"
    "ml`\n\n    One member of a TOML table: its key and its value.\n\n    - `key`: the member's name, one key"
    " part (a dotted key `a.b` is a member `a` holding a table with a member `b`).\n    - `value`: its val"
    "ue.\n\n    Fields:\n        String key\n        Toml value\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}TomlDateKind\u{1f}enum\u{1f}expor"
    "t enum TomlDateKind\u{1f}Which of the four date-time forms a `TomlDateTime` is.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum TomlDateKind"
    "\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    Which of the four date-time forms a `TomlDateTime` is.\n\n    - `To"
    "mlOffsetDateTime`: a date, a time and an offset from UTC: `1979-05-27T07:32:00Z`, `…-08:00`.\n    -"
    " `TomlLocalDateTime`: a date and a time with no offset: `1979-05-27T07:32:00`.\n    - `TomlLocalDate`"
    ": a date alone: `1979-05-27`.\n    - `TomlLocalTime`: a time alone: `07:32:00`.\n\n    Variants:\n      "
    "  TomlOffsetDateTime\n        TomlLocalDateTime\n        TomlLocalDate\n        TomlLocalTime\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::en"
    "coding::toml\u{1f}TomlDateTime\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct TomlDateTime\u{1f}A TOML date-time: the fields of RFC 3339"
    "'s form, and `kind`, which of the four forms it is.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct TomlDateTime\n    in `std::encodin"
    "g::toml`\n\n    A TOML date-time: the fields of RFC 3339's form, and `kind`, which of the four forms i"
    "t is.\n\n    - `kind`: the form; the fields a form does not have are 0.\n    - `year`, `month`, `day`: "
    "the date (`month` 1 to 12, `day` 1 to the month's length).\n    - `hour`, `minute`, `second`: the tim"
    "e (`second` up to 60 for a leap second).\n    - `nanoseconds`: the fraction of the second, 0 to 999 9"
    "99 999; digits beyond nine are dropped when read.\n    - `offset_minutes`: the offset from UTC in min"
    "utes, `-1439` to `1439`; 0 for every other form.\n\n    A plain struct, assigned by copying. `TomlDate"
    "Time::text` writes it as the format does.\n\n    Fields:\n        TomlDateKind kind\n        i64 year\n  "
    "      u8 month\n        u8 day\n        u8 hour\n        u8 minute\n        u8 second\n        u32 nanose"
    "conds\n        i32 offset_minutes\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::parse(StringVi"
    "ew text) : Result<Toml, ParseError>\u{1f}The TOML document `text` holds, as a table.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::par"
    "se(StringView text) : Result<Toml, ParseError>\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The TOML document `"
    "text` holds, as a table.\n\n    The whole of TOML 1.0: tables and arrays of tables under headers, dott"
    "ed keys, inline tables, the four\n    string forms with every escape, integers in decimal, hexadecima"
    "l, octal and binary with underscores,\n    floats with `inf` and `nan`, and the four date-time forms."
    " An empty document is an empty table.\n\n    - `Err(Invalid(i))` at the first byte that does not fit; "
    "at a key or a table header's name that is\n      defined twice or would add to a table the format has"
    " closed (one defined by an earlier header, or an\n      inline table); or at a date or time with a fi"
    "eld beyond its range (a month 13, a 30 February, an hour\n      24). `Toml::describe_error` says whic"
    "h, for a message: `line 3, column 1: name is defined twice`.\n    - `Err(OutOfRange)` for an integer "
    "beyond `i64`, a float beyond `f64`, or tables and arrays nested deeper\n      than 512: each array an"
    "d inline table is one level, and so is each part of a header or a dotted key\n      (`[a.b]` and `a.b"
    " = 1` are two).\n\n    `Err(Empty)` never occurs: a document with no key is an empty table.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::enc"
    "oding::toml\u{1f}Toml::describe_error\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::describe_error(ref<ParseError, shared> e, String"
    "View text) : String\u{1f}The error `Toml::parse(text)` gave, as a message for a person: `ParseError::desc"
    "ribe`'s, with TOML's reason.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::describe_error(ref<ParseError, shared> e, StringView t"
    "ext) : String\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The error `Toml::parse(text)` gave, as a message for"
    " a person: `ParseError::describe`'s, with TOML's reason.\n\n    `line 3, column 1: name is defined twi"
    "ce` for a key or a table defined twice (or added to a table the\n    format has closed); `line 1, col"
    "umn 7: 2026-13-01 is not a date or time (a field beyond its range)` for a\n    month 13; otherwise `P"
    "arseError::describe(e, text)`. `e` is the error `Toml::parse` gave for `text`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml"
    "\u{1f}TomlDateTime::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TomlDateTime::text(ref<TomlDateTime, shared> d) : String\u{1f}The date-t"
    "ime as TOML (and RFC 3339) writes it: the date, `T`, the time, its fraction when there is one, and t"
    "he offset as `Z` or `±HH:MM`; a local form leaves out what it does not have.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TomlDateTim"
    "e::text(ref<TomlDateTime, shared> d) : String\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The date-time as TOM"
    "L (and RFC 3339) writes it: the date, `T`, the time, its fraction when there is one,\n    and the off"
    "set as `Z` or `±HH:MM`; a local form leaves out what it does not have.\n\n    Example, \"TomlDateTime:"
    ":text: the four forms\":\n        String text = \"a = 1979-05-27T07:32:00.999999Z\\nb = 1979-05-27T00:32"
    ":00.5-07:00\\nc = 1979-05-27T07:32:00\\nd = 1979-05-27\\ne = 07:32:00\\n\";\n        Toml doc = Result::un"
    "wrap(Toml::parse(&text));\n        assert(Toml::text(&doc) == text);\n        TomlDateTime b = Option:"
    ":unwrap(Toml::as_datetime(Option::unwrap(Toml::get(&doc, \"b\"))));\n        assert(b.nanoseconds == 50"
    "0000000 && b.offset_minutes == -420 && TomlDateTime::text(&b) == \"1979-05-27T00:32:00.5-07:00\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}s"
    "td::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::text(ref<Toml, shared> t) : String\u{1f}The value `t` as"
    " TOML text.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::text(ref<Toml, shared> t) : String\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    Th"
    "e value `t` as TOML text.\n\n    A table is written as a document: its plain members as `key = value` "
    "lines, then each member that is a\n    table under a `[header]`, and each non-empty array of tables u"
    "nder `[[headers]]`, in order, recursively; a\n    key is bare when it can be and quoted otherwise. St"
    "rings are basic strings with `\"`, `\\` and the control\n    characters escaped; a float is written in "
    "the shortest digits that read back as it, with `inf` and `nan`;\n    a date-time as `TomlDateTime::te"
    "xt` writes it. A value that is not a table is written in the form it takes\n    after `=`: arrays as "
    "`[a, b]`, inline tables as `{ k = v }`. Comments are not kept. `Toml::parse` of the text\n    gives `"
    "t` back, the plain members of each table before its sub-tables.\n\n    Example, \"Toml::text: the layou"
    "t\":\n        Toml doc = Result::unwrap(Toml::parse(\"[server]\\nhost = \\\"example.org\\\"\\nports = [80, 44"
    "3]\\n[server.tls]\\ncert = 'a b'\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"ann\\\"\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"bob\\\"\\n\"));\n        S"
    "tring t = Toml::text(&doc);\n        assert(t == \"[server]\\nhost = \\\"example.org\\\"\\nports = [80, 443]"
    "\\n\\n[server.tls]\\ncert = \\\"a b\\\"\\n\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"ann\\\"\\n\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"bob\\\"\\n\");\n    "
    "    assert(Toml::text(&Result::unwrap(Toml::parse(&t))) == t);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}ex"
    "port fn Toml::get(ref<Toml, shared> t, StringView key) : Option<ref<Toml, shared>> from t\u{1f}The value "
    "of the member named `key` when `t` is a table, else `None`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::get(ref<Toml, shared> t"
    ", StringView key) : Option<ref<Toml, shared>> from t\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The value of "
    "the member named `key` when `t` is a table, else `None`.\n\n    `None` also when there is no such memb"
    "er.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::at\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::at(ref<Toml, shared> t, usize i) : Option<ref<"
    "Toml, shared>>\u{1f}Element `i` of `t` when `t` is an array, else `None`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::at(ref<Toml, s"
    "hared> t, usize i) : Option<ref<Toml, shared>>\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    Element `i` of `t` "
    "when `t` is an array, else `None`.\n\n    `None` also when `i` is past the end.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}"
    "Toml::lookup\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::lookup(ref<Toml, shared> t, StringView path) : Option<ref<Toml, shar"
    "ed>> from t\u{1f}The value at the dotted `path` below `t`: `Toml::lookup(&doc, \"database.ports.0\")`.\u{1f}\u{1f}exp"
    "ort fn Toml::lookup(ref<Toml, shared> t, StringView path) : Option<ref<Toml, shared>> from t\n    in "
    "`std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The value at the dotted `path` below `t`: `Toml::lookup(&doc, \"database.p"
    "orts.0\")`.\n\n    Each part of the path names a member of a table, or, where the value reached is an a"
    "rray, an element by\n    its index written in decimal. `None` when any part is not there. A key that "
    "itself contains a dot is\n    reached with `Toml::get`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::as_text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export"
    " fn Toml::as_text(ref<Toml, shared> t) : Option<StringView>\u{1f}The string `t` holds as a view, or `None"
    "` when `t` is not `TomlString`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_text(ref<Toml, shared> t) : Option<StringView>\n "
    "   in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The string `t` holds as a view, or `None` when `t` is not `TomlStri"
    "ng`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::as_i64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_i64(ref<Toml, shared> t) : Option<i64>"
    "\u{1f}The integer `t` holds, or `None` when `t` is not `TomlInteger`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_i64(ref<Toml, s"
    "hared> t) : Option<i64>\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The integer `t` holds, or `None` when `t` "
    "is not `TomlInteger`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::as_f64\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_f64(ref<Toml, shared>"
    " t) : Option<f64>\u{1f}The float `t` holds, or `None` when `t` is not `TomlFloat`; an integer is not conv"
    "erted.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_f64(ref<Toml, shared> t) : Option<f64>\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    "
    "The float `t` holds, or `None` when `t` is not `TomlFloat`; an integer is not converted.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::enco"
    "ding::toml\u{1f}Toml::as_bool\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_bool(ref<Toml, shared> t) : Option<bool>\u{1f}The boolean "
    "`t` holds, or `None` when `t` is not `TomlBool`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_bool(ref<Toml, shared> t) : Opt"
    "ion<bool>\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The boolean `t` holds, or `None` when `t` is not `TomlBo"
    "ol`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::as_datetime\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_datetime(ref<Toml, shared> t) : O"
    "ption<TomlDateTime>\u{1f}The date-time `t` holds, or `None` when `t` is not `TomlDateTime`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn To"
    "ml::as_datetime(ref<Toml, shared> t) : Option<TomlDateTime>\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The da"
    "te-time `t` holds, or `None` when `t` is not `TomlDateTime`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::as_array\u{1f}fn"
    "\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_array(ref<Toml, shared> t) : Option<ref<Vec<Toml>, shared>>\u{1f}The elements of `t` "
    "when it is an array, or `None` for another kind of value.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_array(ref<Toml, shared"
    "> t) : Option<ref<Vec<Toml>, shared>>\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The elements of `t` when it "
    "is an array, or `None` for another kind of value.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::as_table\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn "
    "Toml::as_table(ref<Toml, shared> t) : Option<ref<Vec<TomlMember>, shared>>\u{1f}The members of `t`, in or"
    "der, when it is a table, or `None` for another kind of value.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::as_table(ref<Toml, sh"
    "ared> t) : Option<ref<Vec<TomlMember>, shared>>\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The members of `t`"
    ", in order, when it is a table, or `None` for another kind of value.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::set"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::set(ref<Toml, exclusive> t, StringView key, Toml v)\u{1f}Sets member `key` of the tab"
    "le `t` to `v`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::set(ref<Toml, exclusive> t, StringView key, Toml v)\n    in `std::enc"
    "oding::toml`\n\n    Sets member `key` of the table `t` to `v`.\n\n    The member of that name is replace"
    "d, or else a new member appended. Faults (`diag.assert-failed`) when\n    `t` is not a table.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::push\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::push(ref<Toml, exclusive> t, Toml v)\u{1f}Appends `v` to the"
    " array `t`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::push(ref<Toml, exclusive> t, Toml v)\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    "
    "Appends `v` to the array `t`.\n\n    Faults (`diag.assert-failed`) when `t` is not an array.\n\n    Exam"
    "ple, \"Toml::set: building a document\":\n        Toml doc = TomlTable(Vec::new());\n        Toml::set(&"
    "mut doc, \"name\", TomlString(\"demo\"));\n        Toml ports = TomlArray(Vec::new());\n        Toml::push"
    "(&mut ports, TomlInteger(8080));\n        Toml::push(&mut ports, TomlInteger(8081));\n        Toml ser"
    "ver = TomlTable(Vec::new());\n        Toml::set(&mut server, \"ports\", ports);\n        Toml::set(&mut "
    "server, \"debug\", TomlBool(false));\n        Toml::set(&mut doc, \"server\", server);\n        Toml::set("
    "&mut doc, \"name\", TomlString(\"demo 2\"));\n        assert(Toml::text(&doc) == \"name = \\\"demo 2\\\"\\n\\n[s"
    "erver]\\nports = [8080, 8081]\\ndebug = false\\n\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}CompressError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum Comp"
    "ressError\u{1f}Why a stream could not be decompressed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum CompressError\n    in `std::compress`\n"
    "\n    Why a stream could not be decompressed.\n\n    - `Corrupt(i)`: the stream is not DEFLATE (or not "
    "the wrapper asked for), or its checksum does not match,\n      first seen at byte `i`.\n    - `Truncat"
    "ed`: the stream ends before its last block or its trailer.\n    - `Oversize`: the output would exceed"
    " the `max` given.\n\n    Variants:\n        Corrupt(usize)\n        Truncated\n        Oversize\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::co"
    "mpress\u{1f}CompressError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CompressError::text(ref<CompressError, shared> e) : str\u{1f}A sh"
    "ort description of `e` for a message, such as `corrupt compressed data`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CompressError::t"
    "ext(ref<CompressError, shared> e) : str\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    A short description of `e` for a"
    " message, such as `corrupt compressed data`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}inflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn inflate(slice<u8, "
    "shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\u{1f}The bytes a raw DEFLATE stream (RFC 1951, "
    "no header or checksum) encodes, at most `max` of them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn inflate(slice<u8, shared> data, us"
    "ize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    The bytes a raw DEFLATE stream"
    " (RFC 1951, no header or checksum) encodes, at most `max` of them.\n\n    `Err(Oversize)` as soon as t"
    "he output would exceed `max`: a limit against a small stream that expands\n    without bound. `Err(Tr"
    "uncated)` when `data` ends inside a block; `Err(Corrupt(i))` at byte `i` for a\n    malformed block. "
    "Bytes after the final block are ignored. Reads stored, fixed and dynamic Huffman blocks.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::comp"
    "ress\u{1f}deflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn deflate(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}`data` compressed as a raw DEFLA"
    "TE stream (RFC 1951, no header or checksum).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn deflate(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\n  "
    "  in `std::compress`\n\n    `data` compressed as a raw DEFLATE stream (RFC 1951, no header or checksum"
    ").\n\n    One fixed strategy, so every implementation writes the same bytes: LZ77 over a 32 KiB window"
    ", each block\n    stored, fixed or dynamic Huffman, whichever is shortest. Empty data is one empty bl"
    "ock (`03 00`).\n\n    Example, \"deflate: empty data, and adler32\":\n        Vec<u8> nothing = Vec::new("
    ");\n        Vec<u8> empty = deflate(&nothing);\n        assert(Vec::len(&empty) == 2 && empty[0] == 0x"
    "03 && empty[1] == 0x00);\n        assert(Vec::len(&Result::unwrap(inflate(&empty, 0))) == 0);\n       "
    " assert(adler32(b\"Wikipedia\") == 300286872);\n        assert(adler32(&nothing) == 1);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress"
    "\u{1f}adler32\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn adler32(slice<u8, shared> data) : u32\u{1f}The Adler-32 checksum of `data` (RFC 195"
    "0), zlib's checksum; 1 for no bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn adler32(slice<u8, shared> data) : u32\n    in `std::c"
    "ompress`\n\n    The Adler-32 checksum of `data` (RFC 1950), zlib's checksum; 1 for no bytes.\n\n    For "
    "CRC-32, gzip's checksum, use `crc32` in `std::crypto`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}zlib_deflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn zli"
    "b_deflate(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}`data` compressed as a zlib stream (RFC 1950): a two-byt"
    "e header, the DEFLATE stream, the Adler-32.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn zlib_deflate(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8"
    ">\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    `data` compressed as a zlib stream (RFC 1950): a two-byte header, the "
    "DEFLATE stream, the Adler-32.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}zlib_inflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn zlib_inflate(slice<u8, share"
    "d> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\u{1f}The bytes a zlib stream encodes, at most `max` "
    "of them, its header checked and its checksum verified.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn zlib_inflate(slice<u8, shared> dat"
    "a, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    The bytes a zlib stream e"
    "ncodes, at most `max` of them, its header checked and its checksum verified.\n\n    `Err(Corrupt(0))` "
    "for a header that is not DEFLATE without a preset dictionary; `Err(Corrupt(i))` at the\n    trailer w"
    "hen the Adler-32 does not match; `Err(Truncated)` for fewer than 6 bytes or a missing trailer;\n    o"
    "therwise as `inflate`, `Err(Oversize)` included.\n\n    Example, \"zlib_inflate: a wrong checksum\":\n   "
    "     Vec<u8> z = zlib_deflate(b\"hello hello hello\");\n        usize last = Vec::len(&z) - 1;\n        "
    "z[last] = z[last] ^ 1;\n        match (zlib_inflate(&z, 100))\n        {\n            Err(Corrupt(at)) "
    ": assert(at == last - 3),\n            _                : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}gz"
    "ip\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn gzip(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}`data` compressed as a gzip file (RFC 1952), "
    "with no name, time or extra fields in its header.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn gzip(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\n"
    "    in `std::compress`\n\n    `data` compressed as a gzip file (RFC 1952), with no name, time or extra"
    " fields in its header.\n\n    The trailer holds the CRC-32 and the length of `data` modulo 2 to the po"
    "wer 32.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}gunzip\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn gunzip(slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u"
    "8>, CompressError>\u{1f}The bytes a gzip file encodes, every member in turn, at most `max` of them.\u{1f}\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn gunzip(slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\n    in `std::compre"
    "ss`\n\n    The bytes a gzip file encodes, every member in turn, at most `max` of them.\n\n    Each heade"
    "r's optional fields are skipped, and zero bytes after the last member (a tape's or a device's\n    pa"
    "dding) are the end. Each member is decoded apart, as gzip does: a distance into an earlier member's\n"
    "    output is `Corrupt`. `Err(Corrupt(i))` at a header that is not gzip's, or at a trailer whose CRC"
    "-32 or\n    length does not match; `Err(Truncated)` for a member cut short; otherwise as `inflate`, `"
    "Err(Oversize)`\n    included.\n\n    Example, \"gunzip: round trip and the size limit\":\n        Vec<u8> "
    "data = Vec::filled(1000, b'a');\n        Vec<u8> packed = gzip(&data);\n        assert(Vec::len(&packe"
    "d) < 100);\n        Vec<u8> back = Result::unwrap(gunzip(&packed, 1000));\n        assert(Vec::len(&ba"
    "ck) == 1000 && back[999] == b'a');\n        match (gunzip(&packed, 999))\n        {\n            Err(Ov"
    "ersize) : {},\n            _             : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}NulError\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export"
    " struct NulError\u{1f}The error of text that holds a NUL byte, which C would take as its end.\u{1f}\u{1f}export str"
    "uct NulError\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The error of text that holds a NUL byte, which C would take as i"
    "ts end.\n\n    `offset` is the position of the first NUL.\n\n    Fields:\n        usize offset\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi"
    "\u{1f}NulError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn NulError::text(ref<NulError, shared> e) : str\u{1f}A short description of th"
    "e error for messages: `\"holds a NUL byte\"`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn NulError::text(ref<NulError, shared> e) : str"
    "\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    A short description of the error for messages: `\"holds a NUL byte\"`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "ffi\u{1f}CString\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct CString\u{1f}Text followed by one NUL byte, for a C function that takes "
    "`const char *`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct CString\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    Text followed by one NUL byte, for a C"
    " function that takes `const char *`.\n\n    Made by `CString::new` or `CString::from_bytes`, which ref"
    "use text that already holds a NUL. `CString::ptr` is\n    the address to pass; it stays valid while t"
    "he `CString` lives, even if the `CString` itself is moved, and\n    dropping the `CString` frees the "
    "bytes. The C function must not write through the address or keep it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::from_bytes\u{1f}"
    "fn\u{1f}export fn CString::from_bytes(slice<u8, shared> b) : Result<CString, NulError>\u{1f}`b` with a NUL byt"
    "e after it, or `Err` with the position of the first NUL already in `b`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::from_byt"
    "es(slice<u8, shared> b) : Result<CString, NulError>\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    `b` with a NUL byte after"
    " it, or `Err` with the position of the first NUL already in `b`.\n\n    The bytes need not be UTF-8: a"
    " path or a name from another system is often not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::new("
    "StringView s) : Result<CString, NulError>\u{1f}`s` with a NUL byte after it, or `Err` with the position o"
    "f the first NUL already in `s`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::new(StringView s) : Result<CString, NulError>\n  "
    "  in `std::ffi`\n\n    `s` with a NUL byte after it, or `Err` with the position of the first NUL alrea"
    "dy in `s`.\n\n    A literal where a `StringView` is expected is made into one: `CString::new(\"HOME\")`."
    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::ptr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::ptr(ref<CString, shared> c) : rawptr<u8>\u{1f}The address "
    "of the first byte, to pass to C as a `const char *`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::ptr(ref<CString, shared> c)"
    " : rawptr<u8>\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The address of the first byte, to pass to C as a `const char *`"
    ".\n\n    Taking the address is safe; the call that uses it is inside `unsafe`. The address is valid un"
    "til the\n    `CString` is dropped.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::len\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::len(ref<CString, sha"
    "red> c) : usize\u{1f}The length of the text, without the NUL.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::len(ref<CString, shared"
    "> c) : usize\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The length of the text, without the NUL.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::as_"
    "bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::as_bytes(ref<CString, shared> c) : slice<u8, shared>\u{1f}The text without th"
    "e NUL, as bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::as_bytes(ref<CString, shared> c) : slice<u8, shared>\n    in `st"
    "d::ffi`\n\n    The text without the NUL, as bytes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}copy_to_raw\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn copy_to_raw<T: "
    "plain>(slice<T, shared> s, rawptr<T> p)\u{1f}The elements of `s`, plain data, copied to C memory at `p`: "
    "an output buffer a C caller owns (D-0257).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn copy_to_raw<T: plain>(slice<T, shared> s, rawp"
    "tr<T> p)\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The elements of `s`, plain data, copied to C memory at `p`: an outpu"
    "t\n    buffer a C caller owns (D-0257). Called inside `unsafe { }`\n    (`[Trusted-Call]`): the caller"
    " vouches that `p` has room for them and\n    that nothing else uses that memory for the call.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "ffi\u{1f}is_null\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn is_null<T>(rawptr<T> p) : bool\u{1f}Whether `p` is C's `NULL`, the address `null"
    "_rawptr<T>()`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn is_null<T>(rawptr<T> p) : bool\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    Whether `p` is C's `"
    "NULL`, the address `null_rawptr<T>()`.\n\n    C functions return `NULL` for \"none\": `getenv` of a name"
    " that is not set, `fopen` of a file that cannot be\n    opened. Testing for it is safe; reading throu"
    "gh `p` is not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::core\u{1f}Result::map_err\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn Result::map_err<T, E1, E2>(Result<T, E1> r"
    ", fn(E1) : E2 f) : Result<T, E2>\u{1f}Keeps an `Ok` as it is and maps an `Err` through `f`: `match (r) { "
    "Ok(v) : Ok(v), Err(e) : Err(f(e)) }`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn Result::map_err<T, E1, E2>(Result<T, E1> r, fn(E1) : E2 f)"
    " : Result<T, E2>\n    in `std::core`\n\n    Keeps an `Ok` as it is and maps an `Err` through `f`: `matc"
    "h (r) { Ok(v) : Ok(v), Err(e) : Err(f(e)) }`.\n    It is the step that turns a library's error into a"
    " program's own before `?` passes it on. `r` is\n    consumed; `f` runs only for an `Err`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}p"
    "rintf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn printf(str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Writes the arguments to standard output as the forma"
    "t `f` says (`spec/21` §2f, `rule.stdlib.format`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn printf(str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::io`\n\n"
    "    Writes the arguments to standard output as the format `f` says (`spec/21` §2f, `rule.stdlib.for"
    "mat`).\n    `f` is a string literal, so the format and the arguments are checked when the program is "
    "compiled and\n    nothing about it can fail at run time. The conversions are C's: `%d` for any intege"
    "r type (there is no\n    `%ld`), `%u`, `%x`, `%X`, `%o`, `%b` (binary) for an integer's bits in its o"
    "wn width, `%f`, `%e`, `%g` for\n    `f32` and `f64`, `%s` for a `str`, a `StringView`, a `ref<String,"
    " shared>` or a `bool`, and `%v` for any printable value\n    or enum \"as CobaltC writes it\" (an enum'"
    "s variant name; a float that reads back as the same value). Width\n    and precision may be `*`, taki"
    "ng the next argument (a `usize`). A reference to a number, a `bool` or a\n    `str` prints as what it"
    " refers to, so `foreach (x in &v) { printf(\"%d\\n\", x); }` prints the elements.\n    Output is buffere"
    "d (D-0178) and written out when the buffer fills, at `flush_stdout()`, and when the\n    program ends"
    ".\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}eprintf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn eprintf(str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Writes the arguments to standard erro"
