    "io`\n\n    Writes the arguments to standard error as the format `f` says, with `printf`'s conversions."
    " For\n    messages that are not the program's output: errors, warnings, progress. Standard error is w"
    "ritten at\n    once, with nothing held back, so its text and standard output's interleave in the orde"
    "r the calls ran\n    (after a `flush_stdout()`, exactly).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}sprintf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn sprintf("
    "str f, a1, …, an) : String\u{1f}The text `printf` would write for the same arguments, as a new `String`"
    " instead of output.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn sprintf(str f, a1, …, an) : String\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The text `print"
    "f` would write for the same arguments, as a new `String` instead of output. The format is\n    checke"
    "d when the program is compiled, as `printf`'s is.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::appendf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn String:"
    ":appendf(ref<String, exclusive> s, str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Appends to `*s` the text `printf` would write"
    " for the same arguments; `String::append` of `sprintf`'s result, without the intermediate `String`.\u{1f}"
    "\u{1f}fn String::appendf(ref<String, exclusive> s, str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Appends to"
    " `*s` the text `printf` would write for the same arguments; `String::append` of `sprintf`'s\n    resu"
    "lt, without the intermediate `String`. The common way to build a line piece by piece before printing"
    "\n    or keeping it once.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}File::printf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn File::printf(ref<File, exclusive> f, "
    "str format, a1, …, an) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Writes the formatted text to the open file `*f`, "
    "as `printf` would to standard output (D-0059); the format is checked when the program is compiled.\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "fn File::printf(ref<File, exclusive> f, str format, a1, …, an) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `s"
    "td::io`\n\n    Writes the formatted text to the open file `*f`, as `printf` would to standard output ("
    "D-0059); the\n    format is checked when the program is compiled. A write that fails is the `Err`, as"
    " for `File::write`.\n    `File` itself is `std::fs`'s type; this function is registered with the `pri"
    "ntf` family in `std::io`,\n    and `import std;` brings in both.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpStream::printf\u{1f}built i"
    "n fn\u{1f}fn TcpStream::printf(ref<TcpStream, exclusive> s, str format, a1, …, an) : Result<void, NetEr"
    "ror>\u{1f}Writes the formatted text to the connected stream `*s`, as `File::printf` does to a file; the w"
    "hole text is written or the `Err` says why (`[Stream-Write]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn TcpStream::printf(ref<TcpStream, "
    "exclusive> s, str format, a1, …, an) : Result<void, NetError>\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Writes the fo"
    "rmatted text to the connected stream `*s`, as `File::printf` does to a file; the whole text\n    is w"
    "ritten or the `Err` says why (`[Stream-Write]`). A line protocol's reply in one call:\n    `TcpStream"
    "::printf(&mut c, \"%d %s\\r\\n\", code, text)?`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::core\u{1f}assert\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn assert(bool c), fn as"
    "sert(bool c, str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Checks `c` and, if it is false, faults with `diag.assert-failed`, r"
    "eporting the formatted message if one is given (`spec/18` §1a, `rule.fail.assert`, D-0065).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn ass"
    "ert(bool c), fn assert(bool c, str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::core`\n\n    Checks `c` and, if it is "
    "false, faults with `diag.assert-failed`, reporting the formatted message if one\n    is given (`spec/"
    "18` §1a, `rule.fail.assert`, D-0065). The message's arguments are evaluated only when the\n    asser"
    "tion fails. An assertion is part of the program's meaning: there is no build in which it is left\n   "
    " out, and `--check` sees its format as it sees `printf`'s. The fault unwinds like any other, so\n    "
    "destructors run and a supervised task reports it to its parent.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}exit\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn e"
    "xit(u8 status) : never\u{1f}Ends the program with exit status `status` (`[Exit]`, `spec/21` §2k, D-0150)"
