    "y conforming implementation gives the same bits.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn sqrt(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The squar"
    "e root of `x`, correctly rounded (`[Float-Fn]`, `spec/21` §3d, D-0091): every conforming\n    implem"
    "entation gives the same bits. A NaN for a negative `x`; `-0.0` for `-0.0`; a NaN in gives a NaN out."
    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}floor\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn floor(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to an integral value toward negative in"
    "finity, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn floor(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to an integra"
    "l value toward negative infinity, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`). A NaN or an infinity is\n    returned as it"
    " is.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}ceil\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn ceil(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to an integral value toward positive "
    "infinity, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn ceil(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to an integr"
    "al value toward positive infinity, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}round\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn round(T "
    "x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to the nearest integral value, halfway cases away from zero (`2.5` to `3.0`, `-2."
    "5` to `-3.0`), exactly (`[Float-Fn]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn round(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to the"
    " nearest integral value, halfway cases away from zero (`2.5` to `3.0`, `-2.5` to\n    `-3.0`), exactl"
    "y (`[Float-Fn]`). Convert the result with `rule.arith.convert` when an integer is wanted.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::mat"
    "h\u{1f}trunc\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn trunc(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to an integral value toward zero, exactly (`[Float"
    "-Fn]`): the fractional part dropped.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn trunc(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to an in"
    "tegral value toward zero, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`): the fractional part dropped.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}ln\u{1f}built "
    "in fn\u{1f}fn ln(T x) : T\u{1f}The natural logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place of the mathemat"
    "ical value (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0101): the platform's C library computes it, so the result i"
    "s the same on one platform and may differ in the last bit between platforms.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn ln(T x) : T\n    in "
    "`std::math`\n\n    The natural logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place of the mathematical"
    " value\n    (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0101): the platform's C library computes it, so the result i"
    "s the same on one\n    platform and may differ in the last bit between platforms. A NaN for a negativ"
    "e `x`; negative infinity for\n    `±0`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}exp\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn exp(T x) : T\u{1f}`e` to the power"
    " `x`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn exp(T x) : T\n    in `std::ma"
